window.SEED_QUESTIONS = [{"id":"seed-001","question":"_____ are daily opportunities that occur when you are with your adolescents.","answer":"Teachable moments","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-002","question":"About what share of older people faced difficulties accessing healthcare services when needed? — _____.","answer":"About one-fifth","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-003","question":"_____ are social associations, connections, or affiliations between two or more people.","answer":"Interpersonal relationships","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-004","question":"Among those aware, what percentages had received pneumococcal and influenza vaccines, respectively? — _____.","answer":"55% and 57%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-005","question":"_____ have a social networking account in Filipino youth.","answer":"53%","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-006","question":"Among those who fell, what was the average number of falls in the past year? — _____.","answer":"Two falls","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-007","question":"_____ is all about choosing between two or more courses of action.","answer":"Decision-making","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-008","question":"Based on WHO-5, what share experienced positive feelings more than half of the time in the prior 2 weeks? — _____.","answer":"Over 70%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-009","question":"_____ is one which is collected for the first time by the researcher.","answer":"Primary data","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-010","question":"How many respondents were in the Wave 1 sample? — _____.","answer":"5,985 respondents","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-011","question":"_____ is the foundation of your life. You have the power and choice to build your life to what you want it to be.","answer":"Self-esteem","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-012","question":"How many Wave 1 respondents were still alive at Wave 2? — _____.","answer":"4,397","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-013","question":"_____ means caring deeply for that person and being committed to his or her well-being and happiness.","answer":"Loving someone","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-014","question":"What is the common marital status of surviving older women? — _____.","answer":"Widowed","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-015","question":"_____ produce perspiration that is clear and odorless. These glands start working as soon as you are born.","answer":"Eccrine glands","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-016","question":"_____ is a key determinant of fertility.","answer":"Contraceptive use","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-017","question":"_____ such as pills, injectable are drugs that contain hormones (estrogen and progestogen) similar to those found in a woman’s body.","answer":"Combined Hormonal Contraceptives","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-018","question":"Data collection for the 2018 National Migration Survey ended in _____.","answer":"November","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-019","question":"After ovulation, the follicle is transformed into the _____, which produces an increasing amount of the hormone called progesterone.","answer":"corpus luteum","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-020","question":"What percentage experienced a moderate decline in food intake? — _____.","answer":"25%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-021","question":"Countries recognize that _____ is imperative in sustainable development initiatives.","answer":"youth involvement","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-022","question":"Based on the 2022 NDHS, unmet need for FP declined from 16.7% to _____ between 2017 and 2022.","answer":"12.4%","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-023","question":"Day 4 of pregnancy is _____.","answer":"Morula","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-024","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of first-time international migrants cited employment as a reason.","answer":"89%","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-025","question":"Excessive use and time invested on internet leads to _____.","answer":"internet addiction","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-026","question":"Feature of Census where all persons are enumerated separately and the characteristics of all persons are also recorded separately — _____.","answer":"Individual Enumeration","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-027","question":"From puberty onwards, males continue to produce ______ in their testicles or testes.","answer":"sperm","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-028","question":"What percentage had difficulty lifting an object weighing approximately 10 kg? — _____.","answer":"44%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-029","question":"In fostering your cognitive development be CRITICAL of things around you – thinking before doing. C stand for _____.","answer":"Critically think","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-030","question":"Presidential Decree No. _____ (s. 1972) established the Commission on Population (POPCOM).","answer":"79","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-031","question":"In nurturing intimacy, express your love in a healthy way and open yourself to BE LOVED. L stand for _____.","answer":"Love yourself","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-032","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of international migrant remittance flows came from Asia.","answer":"65%","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-033","question":"Overall, complications from _____ is one of the main causes of maternal deaths.","answer":"unsafe abortion","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-034","question":"In computing the General Fertility Rate (GFR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"1,000","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-035","question":"Poor or negative body image leads to INSECURE self. U stand for _____.","answer":"Unhealthy coping mechanisms","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-036","question":"What percentage lived at least 10 km from the nearest health facility? — _____.","answer":"16%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-037","question":"SHAPE Module _____ deals with adolescents’ changing relationship with family and peers, and their growing interest in sexual relationships.","answer":"3","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-038","question":"The main driver of population growth is _____.","answer":"fertility","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-039","question":"The _____ includes all dry days after the menstrual bleeding stops.","answer":"pre-ovulatory phase","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-040","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of people intending to move planned to go abroad.","answer":"36%","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-041","question":"The _________ is the passageway through from which a man urinates or ejaculates.","answer":"urethra","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-042","question":"In computing the Percent Rural, what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-043","question":"The first time menstruation happens is called “____.”","answer":"menarche","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-044","question":"What percentage of inpatient care before death occurred in public health facilities? — _____.","answer":"59%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-045","question":"The release of egg from the ovary is called _________.","answer":"ovulation","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-046","question":"Women who intend to space or limit births but are not using family planning methods are considered to have an “_____” for family planning.","answer":"unmet need","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-047","question":"The testes are found inside the ________.","answer":"scrotum","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-048","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of children aged 12–23 months received all basic antigens.","answer":"72%","set":"Set 1","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-049","question":"Title of Module 1 of SHAPE is _____.","answer":"Growing Up","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-050","question":"The 2018 NMS reported _____ of lifetime migrants crossed regional boundaries.","answer":"57%","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-051","question":"When a woman is about to give birth, her body enters a stage called “_____.”","answer":"labor","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-052","question":"In computing the Population Growth Rate (PGR) using Exponential Change, what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-053","question":"Early signs of pregnancy differ from woman to woman and between pregnancies. These include: (No. 10) — _____.","answer":"feeling unusually emotional","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-054","question":"What percentage of older Filipinos live alone? — _____.","answer":"12%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-055","question":"Early signs of pregnancy differ from woman to woman and between pregnancies. These include: (No. 7) — _____.","answer":"cramps","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-056","question":"As a consensual union, cohabitation may be a transition to marriage or an _____.","answer":"Alternative to marriage","set":"Set 1","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-057","question":"It is a longing for sexual expression or a feeling of sexual attraction — _____.","answer":"Sexual desire","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-058","question":"The level of fertility at which a population exactly replaces itself from one generation to the next — _____.","answer":"Replacement Fertility Level","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-059","question":"Other term for “wet dreams.” — _____.","answer":"nocturnal emission","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-060","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of households used improved drinking-water sources.","answer":"98%","set":"Set 1","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-061","question":"Percent of adolescents (15-19 years old) who have begun childbearing in 2002 — _____.","answer":"6.9%","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-062","question":"The 2020 PDP pandemic relief initially supported _____ of Filipino families.","answer":"80%","set":"Set 1","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-063","question":"Percentage of youth who do not use protection against unintended pregnancy and STIs according to YAFS4 — _____.","answer":"78%","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-064","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Census of Population and Housing” is _____.","answer":"CPH","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-065","question":"Symptoms: Recurrent episodes of painful sores on genitals or anus — _____.","answer":"Herpes","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-066","question":"In computing the Urban Population Growth Rate (UGR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-067","question":"There are ways to be safe and responsible online, while still having fun. No. 4 — _____.","answer":"Watch your tone","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-068","question":"What percentage of older persons often experience pain? — _____.","answer":"33%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-069","question":"This issue pertains to the habitual or addictive use of alcohol and illegal drugs — _____.","answer":"Substance abuse","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-070","question":"According to the 2022 NDHS, what percentage were in consensual unions? — _____.","answer":"19%","set":"Set 1","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-071","question":"You can build mutually respectful and responsible relationships by. No. 1 — _____.","answer":"Respecting yourself","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-072","question":"A more alarming condition is that the number of registered births among adolescents aged 10-14 years has been _____ from 2016 to 2021, except for 2020 due to the pandemic.","answer":"increasing","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-073","question":"_____ are learned. They are not innate or “natural.” In fact, almost everything that males can do, females can also do. And almost everything that females can do, males can also do.","answer":"Gender roles","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-074","question":"An area's annual population growth rate is abbreviated _____.","answer":"PGR","set":"Set 1","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-075","question":"_____ is a period of transition from childhood to adulthood. It is marked by puberty. It is a time of rapid physical growth that brings about confusion, insecurities, and even fear.","answer":"Adolescence","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-076","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of the household population had PhilHealth coverage.","answer":"70%","set":"Set 1","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-077","question":"A _____ is a way of living that lowers the risk of being seriously ill or dying early (World Health Organization). It helps in keeping and improving people's health and well-being.","answer":"healthy lifestyle","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-078","question":"The PDP cites the Philippines' 2022 Global Innovation Index rank as _____.","answer":"59th","set":"Set 1","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-079","question":"At puberty, the body starts the process of “_____” where boys and girls have become capable of reproduction. It also includes enlargement of primary sex organs.","answer":"sexual maturation","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-080","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Gross Domestic Product” is _____.","answer":"GDP","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-081","question":"Prior to ejaculation, the _____ release a drop or two of fluid through the tip of the penis. This is called pre-ejaculate, and it cleans the urethra.","answer":"Cowper’s glands","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-082","question":"It refers to the number of migrants arriving in an area of destination per 1,000 population of the destination area in a given year — _____.","answer":"In-Migration Rate (InMR)","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-083","question":"The 2017 National Demographic Health Survey conducted by the Philippine Statistics Authority shows that _____ out of 10 young women aged 15 to 19 years old had begun child-bearing.","answer":"1","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-084","question":"What percentage of those who fell required medical treatment? — _____.","answer":"15%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-085","question":"The Parent-Teen Talk is a _____-hour interactive learning experience for at least 10 couples and at least one of their teen children (20 adults and 10 teens).","answer":"4","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-086","question":"Between 2000 and 2010, by what percentage did unmarried couple households increase in the United States? — _____.","answer":"41%","set":"Set 1","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-087","question":"This contraceptive method offer the greatest protection against infection. They are inserted or put on each time the partners have sex — _____.","answer":"Barrier Methods","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-088","question":"Memorandum Circular No. _____: Approving and Adopting the Philippine Population and Development Plan of Action 2023-2028, and Directing the Implementation Thereof","answer":"40","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-089","question":"_____ is a scientific method of observation that gathers non-numerical data. It aims to describe meanings, concepts definitions, characteristics, metaphors, symbols, nature, and events and not to their \"counts or measures.”","answer":"Qualitative research","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-090","question":"The age-specific fertility rate is abbreviated _____.","answer":"ASFR","set":"Set 1","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-091","question":"Among the six major economies in the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), the _____ posed the highest rate of teenage pregnancies and is the only country where this rate has been steadily increasing (Hor, 2014).","answer":"Philippines","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-092","question":"The 2022 NDHS household population with at least basic sanitation service in BARMM was _____.","answer":"55%","set":"Set 1","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-093","question":"The _____ is a highly interactive and participative adult learning strategy that aims to educate and enhance the skills of parents as well as adolescents in a two-way communication about sexual and reproductive health concerns.","answer":"Parent-Teen Talk","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-094","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “Health of women during pregnancy, childbirth and the postnatal period” is _____.","answer":"Maternal health","set":"Set 1","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-095","question":"Pair of thin cutaneous folds that form part of the vulva, or external female genitalia. They function as protective structures that surround the clitoris, urinary orifice, and vaginal orifice — _____.","answer":"Labia minora","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-096","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Interagency Committee on Migration Statistics” is _____.","answer":"IACMS","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-097","question":"This is the ability to think through situations adequately, weighing the advantages and disadvantages so as to be able to make appropriate decisions concerning other people or one's own situation — _____.","answer":"Critical Thinking Skills","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-098","question":"It the type of population pyramid which has a broad base that indicates high fertility — _____.","answer":"Expansive Pyramid","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-099","question":"What percentage received their vaccinations at barangay health stations? — _____.","answer":"82%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-100","question":"How many female participants were part of the study? — _____.","answer":"48 female participants","set":"Set 1","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-101","question":"The majority of Filipinos’ overall health condition has improved over the years as indicated by a _____ mortality rate and an increasing lifespan.","answer":"declining","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-102","question":"The ICPD Programme of Action was agreed to in the year _____.","answer":"1994","set":"Set 1","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-103","question":"The 2022 NDHS rural total fertility rate was _____ children per woman.","answer":"2.2","set":"Set 1","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-104","question":"According to YAFS5, mean age at circumcision was _____ years.","answer":"11","set":"Set 1","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-105","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The annual rate of change or the year-on-year change in the Consumer Price Index. (NSCB Resolution No. 11 Series of 2003)” is _____.","answer":"Inflation rate","set":"Set 1","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-106","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “overseas Filipino workers family circle” is _____.","answer":"OFC","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-107","question":"_____ is feeling good about ourselves and feeling that we are a worthwhile person. It is important because it shows ourselves how we view the way we are and the sense of our personal value. Thus, it affects the way we are and how we behave and relate with others.","answer":"Self-esteem","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-108","question":"It is an estimate of the average number of additional years a person can expect to live after a particular age x, computed also on the life table — _____.","answer":"Life Expectancy","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-109","question":"What percentage report other real estate properties as assets? — _____.","answer":"13%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-110","question":"In this study, romantic motivations were more evident among which participants? — _____.","answer":"Male participants","set":"Set 1","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-111","question":"But now, the country’s population is only growing at a pace of _____ annually. With more than 109 million people, however, the country still occupies the 13th place in the world’s population size (UNDESA, 2022).","answer":"1.6%","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-112","question":"The subgroup actually using project services is population-at-_____.","answer":"demand","set":"Set 1","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-113","question":"The 2022 Philippine NDHS began data collection in the month of _____.","answer":"May","set":"Set 1","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-114","question":"According to YAFS5, the region with the highest rate of youth drinking was _____.","answer":"Central Visayas","set":"Set 1","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-115","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The probability of dying between birth and age five, expressed as the number of deaths below age five per 1,000 live births during a given period” is _____.","answer":"Under-five mortality rate","set":"Set 1","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-116","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Philippine Statistics Authority” is _____.","answer":"PSA","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-117","question":"A _____ gives teenagers a safe place to socialize and hangout and reduces the chances that they will engage in criminal behavior, according to a 2011 article published in the American Journal of Community Psychology. It also helps reduce the chances that teens will engage in other risky activities, such as unprotected sex and alcohol use.","answer":"teen center","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-118","question":"It is the rate computed for a disaggregated population on the basis of a selected characteristic or certain characteristics. It uses a specific subgroup of population as denominator — _____.","answer":"Specific Rate","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-119","question":"What percentage reported no decrease in food intake in the 3 months before the interview? — _____.","answer":"73%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-120","question":"What kind of misunderstandings did many couples describe as normal? — _____.","answer":"Common everyday misunderstandings","set":"Set 1","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-121","question":"The growing ageing population during the _____ phase of the demographic transition can create a slowdown in the country’s economic growth as the number of consumers (the older population) grows faster compared to productive workers.","answer":"third","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-122","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “refers to the subgroup of population-at-risk exhibiting the problem condition” is _____.","answer":"Population-at-need","set":"Set 1","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-123","question":"Percentage of women who use any contraceptive method — _____.","answer":"Contraceptive prevalence","set":"Set 1","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-124","question":"The 2021 population of Filipino female youth aged 15–24 was _____ million.","answer":"9.8","set":"Set 1","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-125","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “Constituents of the atmosphere that contribute to the greenhouse effect including, but not limited to, carbon dioxide, methane, nitrous oxide, hydrofluorocarbons, perfluorocarbons and sulfur hexafluoride. (RA 9729, 2009)” is _____.","answer":"Greenhouse gases","set":"Set 1","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-126","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Social Security System” is _____.","answer":"SSS","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-127","question":"Humans have an XY sex-determination system: the Y chromosome carries factors responsible for male development. The \"_____,\" in the absence of a Y chromosome, is female-like. Males typically have an X and a Y chromosome (XY), and females with two X chromosomes (XX).","answer":"default sex","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-128","question":"It refers to the time interval for which the measure is being computed. This is usually a calendar year. Thus, the derive measure denotes occurrence or condition in an annual basis — _____.","answer":"Period","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-129","question":"What percentage were bedridden within 2 weeks before the survey? — _____.","answer":"4%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-130","question":"What practical family responsibility can cohabitation help partners share? — _____.","answer":"Child rearing","set":"Set 1","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-131","question":"A form of spatial or geographic mobility of people involving a change of usual place of residence between clearly defined geographic or political units (such as regions, province and city/municipality for _____) during a specified period of observation for a reason such as economic, social, political and cultural. (PSA Board Resolution No. 08 series of 2017)","answer":"internal migration","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-132","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “this involves a majority of the constituents being consulted on certain issue/s” is _____.","answer":"General Assemblies","set":"Set 1","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-133","question":"On the NDHS 2022 drinking-water service ladder, the level described as “Drinking water from an improved source, and round-trip collection time is more than 30 minutes” is _____.","answer":"Limited","set":"Set 1","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-134","question":"The fifth Young Adult Fertility and Sexuality Study is abbreviated _____.","answer":"YAFS5","set":"Set 1","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-135","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The gap between individuals, households, businesses and geographic areas at different socio-economic levels with regard to both their opportunities to access information and communication technologies (ICTs) and to their use of the” is _____.","answer":"Digital Divide","set":"Set 1","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-136","question":"The factors that attract people to a particular place are _____.","answer":"pull factors","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-137","question":"Standard Days Method (SDM) is based on calculated fertile and infertile periods for menstrual cycles that range from _____ days. This method uses a device, color-coded “cycle beads” to mark the fertile and infertile days of the menstrual cycle.","answer":"26 to 32","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-138","question":"It is the number of children under age five per 1,000 women of childbearing age in a given year. It is used as a rough fertility indicator, especially when detailed data on births are lacking — _____.","answer":"Child-Woman Ratio (CWR)","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-139","question":"What share of older Filipinos take care of their grandchildren fully or partially? — _____.","answer":"About one-fourth","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-140","question":"What thematic analysis approach is cited for generating overarching themes? — _____.","answer":"Reflexive thematic analysis","set":"Set 1","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-141","question":"The pattern of growing number of females migrating within and across the regions globally is referred to as the “_____”. This has become a distinctive feature of the migratory patterns in the Western Pacific Region (UN ESCAP Asia-Pacific Migration Report 2020).","answer":"feminization of migration","set":"Set 1","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-142","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The total number of population belonging to ages 65 and above for every 100 population of working age” is _____.","answer":"Old dependency ratio","set":"Set 1","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-143","question":"The probability of dying between the first month of life and the first birthday (computed as the difference between infant and neonatal mortality) — _____.","answer":"Postneonatal mortality","set":"Set 1","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-144","question":"YAFS5 reported the ideal age at first childbirth for women as _____ years.","answer":"25","set":"Set 1","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-145","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The strategy for making women's, as well as men's, concerns and experiences the integral dimension of the design, implementation, and monitoring and evaluation of policies and programs in all political, economic, and societal spheres so” is _____.","answer":"Gender mainstreaming","set":"Set 1","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-146","question":"Among those who migrated abroad in the past five years, the top destination countries are _____ (20%) and United Arab Emirates (15 %) followed by Japan (9%), Kuwait and Qatar (7% each), Malaysia (6%), the USA and Taiwan (5% each).","answer":"Saudia Arabia","set":"Set 1","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-147","question":"The _____ is a small organ, shaped like a flower bud with a bit of tissue forming a small “hood.” It contains thousands of nerve endings that make it an extremely sensitive organ. Touch stimulation of the nerve endings in this part produces sensations of sexual pleasure.","answer":"clitoris","set":"Set 1","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-148","question":"Main Source of Data which is a canvass of selected households in a population usually to infer demographic characteristics or trends for a selected person’s interviewed in the sample households — _____.","answer":"Survey","set":"Set 1","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-149","question":"What was the Wave 1 response rate? — _____.","answer":"94%","set":"Set 1","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-150","question":"Which female age group had the highest number in common-law/live-in arrangements? — _____.","answer":"25-29 years old","set":"Set 1","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-151","question":"_____ are fertile continuously from puberty onward.","answer":"Males","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-152","question":"According to GALI, what percentage were severely limited because of health problems? — _____.","answer":"15%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-153","question":"_____ are the only contraceptive method that protects partners from sexually transmitted infections including HIV.","answer":"Condoms","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-154","question":"Among those not vaccinated, what percentage reported that they did not want to be vaccinated? — _____.","answer":"82%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-155","question":"_____ involves sudden or rapid growth or change in the physical body of an adolescent.","answer":"Growth spurt","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-156","question":"Among those who tested positive for COVID-19, what percentage had been hospitalised? — _____.","answer":"20%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-157","question":"_____ is an approach in promoting healthy and positive behaviors among adolescents through their peers.","answer":"Peer Education","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-158","question":"By what year is the Philippines projected to transition to an ageing society? — _____.","answer":"2030","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-159","question":"_____ is the ability of males to provide healthy sperm capable of starting a healthy pregnancy.","answer":"Male fertility","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-160","question":"How many siblings do older Filipinos have on average? — _____.","answer":"About seven siblings","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-161","question":"_____ is the number of live births among adolescents (10-19) per 1,000 adolescents in the locality.","answer":"Adolescent birth rate","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-162","question":"In what year was Ageing and Health in the Philippines: Wave 2 published? — _____.","answer":"2025","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-163","question":"_____ means not expressing your own needs and feelings, or expressing them so weakly that they will not be addressed.","answer":"Passive Communication","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-164","question":"What is the most commonly diagnosed illness among older Filipinos? — _____.","answer":"Hypertension","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-165","question":"_____ refers to people who are attracted to same or opposite sex.","answer":"Bisexual","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-166","question":"_____ is the most preferred area of destination and the Cordillera Administrative Region (CAR) as the least preferred destination.","answer":"CALABARZON","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-167","question":"_____ use the internet in Filipino youth.","answer":"59%","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-168","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of Filipinos ever migrated for at least three months.","answer":"55%","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-169","question":"An _____ connects the placenta to the fetus.","answer":"umbilical cord","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-170","question":"What percentage experienced a severe decline in food intake? — _____.","answer":"2%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-171","question":"CSE stands for _____.","answer":"Comprehensive Sexuality Education","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-172","question":"Demographic transition directly influences the _____ of the population.","answer":"age structure","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-173","question":"Day 5 of pregnancy is _____.","answer":"Early Blastocyst","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-174","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of households had a member abroad at the time of survey.","answer":"9%","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-175","question":"Fear of aversion to homosexuals is called _____.","answer":"homophobia","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-176","question":"In computing the Age Dependency Ratio, what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-177","question":"From the epididymis, the sperm enters the __________.","answer":"vas deferens","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-178","question":"What percentage had difficulty standing or going without sitting for 2 hours? — _____.","answer":"42%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-179","question":"In fostering your cognitive development be CRITICAL of things around you – thinking before doing. C stand for _____. (2nd C)","answer":"Create opportunities","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-180","question":"The _____ (2022) has cited the Philippine economy as one of the most vibrant and dynamic in the Asia Pacific region.","answer":"World Bank","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-181","question":"Menstruation, or _____, signals the beginning of a new cycle.","answer":"menstrual bleeding","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-182","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of international migrants had difficulty after returning home.","answer":"51%","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-183","question":"Poor or negative body image leads to INSECURE self. C stand for _____.","answer":"Comparison with others","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-184","question":"In computing the In- Migration Rate (InMR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"1,000","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-185","question":"Positive peer pressure can be called _____.","answer":"peer support","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-186","question":"What percentage lived at least 10 km from the nearest pharmacy? — _____.","answer":"29%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-187","question":"SHAPE Module _____ focuses on the physiological or physical changes at puberty.","answer":"1","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-188","question":"The population increased at a rate of _____ from 2015-2020 which is slower than the 1.7 annual growth rate between 2010–2015.","answer":"1.6","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-189","question":"The _____ is a small plastic device inserted into a woman’s uterine cavity to prevent pregnancy.","answer":"Intrauterine Device (IUD)","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-190","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of returning migrants received government support.","answer":"4%","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-191","question":"The egg (if it is not fertilized) survives for as long as _____ hours.","answer":"24","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-192","question":"In computing the Percent Urban, what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-193","question":"The growth of your body from childhood to adulthood is known as _____.","answer":"puberty","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-194","question":"What percentage of liabilities are loans from moneylenders? — _____.","answer":"44%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-195","question":"The release of the egg from the ovary is called _____.","answer":"ovulation","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-196","question":"Are statistics referring to births, deaths and marriages — _____.","answer":"Vital Statistics","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-197","question":"The World Health Organization recommends _____ without other food for the first six months of a baby’s life.","answer":"breastfeeding","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-198","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of children aged 24–59 months were developmentally on track.","answer":"77%","set":"Set 2","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-199","question":"Title of Module 3 of SHAPE is _____.","answer":"Changing Relationships","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-200","question":"The 2018 NMS was jointly implemented by the PSA and the _____.","answer":"UPPI","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-201","question":"Women commonly feel nauseous during the first trimester; the nausea is sometimes called “_____.”","answer":"morning sickness","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-202","question":"In computing the Population Growth Rate (PGR) using Geometric Change, what does r stand for? — _____.","answer":"Rate of Growth","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-203","question":"Early signs of pregnancy differ from woman to woman and between pregnancies. These include: (No. 3) — _____.","answer":"sensitive nipples","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-204","question":"What percentage of older Filipinos live with at least one child? — _____.","answer":"59%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-205","question":"Early signs of pregnancy differ from woman to woman and between pregnancies. These include: (No. 8) — _____.","answer":"feeling bloated","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-206","question":"According to the 2017 NDHS, what percentage of women aged 15-49 were living in consensual unions? — _____.","answer":"18%","set":"Set 2","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-207","question":"It is the period when children change to become adults — _____.","answer":"Adolescence","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-208","question":"their place of birth — _____.","answer":"40%","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-209","question":"Percent of adolescents (10-19 years old) who have begun childbearing in 2002 — _____.","answer":"6.3%","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-210","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of live births had skilled assistance during delivery.","answer":"90%","set":"Set 2","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-211","question":"Percent of adolescents (15-19 years old) who have begun childbearing in 2013 — _____.","answer":"13.7%","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-212","question":"The COP26 climate conference referenced in the PDP took place in _____.","answer":"Glasgow","set":"Set 2","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-213","question":"Practical tips in being good and effective parent to adolescents — _____.","answer":"Show genuine love","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-214","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “computer-assisted personal interviewing” is _____.","answer":"CAPI","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-215","question":"Symptoms: Some people experience flu-like symptoms, jaundice, and dark-colored urine; others experience no symptoms — _____.","answer":"Hepatitis B","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-216","question":"In the formula for Crude Birth Rate (CBR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"1,000","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-217","question":"There are ways to be safe and responsible online, while still having fun. No. 5 — _____.","answer":"Be skeptical","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-218","question":"What percentage of surviving older persons had ever tested positive for COVID-19? — _____.","answer":"3%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-219","question":"Wanting to be able to make own decisions, choose friends, plan activities, and make their own dreams — _____.","answer":"Independence","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-220","question":"According to YAFS 2021 cited in the report, how many Filipino youth aged 15-24 were there? — _____.","answer":"About 20 million","set":"Set 2","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-221","question":"You can build mutually respectful and responsible relationships by. No. 5 — _____.","answer":"Nurturing open communication","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-222","question":"Across educational attainment, modern contraceptive use _____ among women with no education while their unmet need for FP declined during the same period.","answer":"increased","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-223","question":"_____ are one-stop-shop facility where adolescents can easily access a wide range of information and services to ensure their health and wellbeing.","answer":"Teen Centers","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-224","question":"Births are the demographic process called _____.","answer":"Fertility","set":"Set 2","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-225","question":"_____ is asking for what you want or expressing how you feel in an honest and respectful way that does not infringe on another person's rights or put the individual down.","answer":"Communicating aggressively","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-226","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of women aged 15–19 had ever been pregnant.","answer":"5%","set":"Set 2","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-227","question":"Adolescents (15-19 years old) have ____ knowledge about the risk of conception and most of them acknowledge their lack of knowledge about sex.","answer":"poor","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-228","question":"The PDP says COVID-19 was the _____ leading cause of mortality in 2021.","answer":"third","set":"Set 2","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-229","question":"Menstruation comes from the Latin word _____, which means “month.” Most females have a period each month. This is why menstruation is also called “monthly period.”","answer":"mensis","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-230","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “health maintenance organization” is _____.","answer":"HMO","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-231","question":"Prior to ejaculation, the Cowper’s glands release a drop or two of fluid through the tip of the penis. This is called _____, and it cleans the urethra.","answer":"pre-ejaculate","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-232","question":"It refers to the number of migrants departing or leaving an area per 1,000 population in that area in a given year — _____.","answer":"Emigration Rate (ER)","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-233","question":"The cells inside the blastocyst will grow into a baby. The cells on the outside join the wall of the uterus and form a protective organ called the “_____.”","answer":"placenta","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-234","question":"What percentage own the house where they currently reside? — _____.","answer":"77%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-235","question":"These unplanned activities can be taken as “_____” or an opportunity where parents can inculcate valuable insight or lesson to their child out of the situation, they are in.","answer":"teachable moments","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-236","question":"How did noncohabiting women describe stories of cohabitation? — _____.","answer":"As cautionary tales","set":"Set 2","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-237","question":"_____ are demonstrations of power over another person. They always violate the human rights of the person they are used against, regardless of whether they express jealousy or other feelings.","answer":"Violence and coercion","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-238","question":"Only _____ in every 10 or 13.3% of children 6-23 months old met the minimum acceptable diet (MAD), indicating poor quality and quantity of complementary foods.","answer":"one / 1","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-239","question":"_____ is determined by five factors present at birth: the presence or absence of a Y chromosome, the type of gonads, the sex hormones, the internal reproductive anatomy (such as the uterus in females), and the external genitalia.","answer":"Biological sex","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-240","question":"The contraceptive prevalence rate is abbreviated _____.","answer":"CPR","set":"Set 2","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-241","question":"An _____ is caused by blood filing the spongy tissue in the penis as a result of sexual stimulation; lifting or straining; dreaming; being cold; wearing tight clothing; feeling fear or excitement; or having a full bladder on waking.","answer":"erection","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-242","question":"The 2022 NDHS household population with at least basic sanitation service in CALABARZON was _____.","answer":"92%","set":"Set 2","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-243","question":"The _____ is a permanent method of contraception for men in which the vas deferens (the tubes that serve as passageway of sperm) are tied and cut or blocked through a small opening on the scrotal skin.","answer":"No-Scalpel Vasectomy (NSV)","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-244","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “is the level of knowledge about financial concepts and principles” is _____.","answer":"Financial Literacy","set":"Set 2","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-245","question":"Symptoms for Women: Most women are asymptomatic; abnormal vaginal discharge or burning sensation when urinating. Symptoms for Men: Men often experience discharge or burning when urinating. Some men have no symptoms — _____.","answer":"Gonorrhea","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-246","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “master sample frame” is _____.","answer":"MSF","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-247","question":"Your capacity to communicate with your parents and other significant persons in your life is important in developing your social skills especially in harnessing your relationship with your parents — _____.","answer":"Communication Skills","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-248","question":"Population Growth Rate = 2.35 — _____.","answer":"29.5 years","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-249","question":"What percentage rely on remittances from children living abroad? — _____.","answer":"18%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-250","question":"How many major motivations for cohabitation are summarized in the study? — _____.","answer":"Eight","set":"Set 2","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-251","question":"While the country has witnessed a significant fertility decline over the last decade, the _____ of the population as well as region-specific fertility rates have not been even.","answer":"geographic distribution","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-252","question":"The infant mortality rate is abbreviated _____.","answer":"IMR","set":"Set 2","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-253","question":"The 2022 NDHS successfully interviewed _____ occupied households.","answer":"30,372","set":"Set 2","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-254","question":"According to YAFS5, mean age at menarche was _____ years.","answer":"13","set":"Set 2","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-255","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The proportion of employed persons to the total labor force. (LFS Technical Notes, PSA)” is _____.","answer":"Employment Rate","set":"Set 2","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-256","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “overseas Filipino workers” is _____.","answer":"OFW","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-257","question":"_____ is the kind of influence that makes you do things that have negative consequences or impact on you and to others. This pressure makes you want to make other people feel bad or sad, or make you do something just so you feel part of the group even when you know that it is wrong.","answer":"Negative peer pressure","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-258","question":"It is simply the number of males per 100 females in a population. This is obtained by dividing the male population by the female population then multiplied by 100 — _____.","answer":"Sex Ratio","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-259","question":"What percentage reported considerable difficulty meeting household expenses? — _____.","answer":"25%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-260","question":"What bridges social structures and social events in the framework? — _____.","answer":"Social practices","set":"Set 2","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-261","question":"But now, the country’s population is only growing at a pace of 1.6% annually. With more than _____ million people, however, the country still occupies the 13th place in the world’s population size (UNDESA, 2022).","answer":"109","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-262","question":"The subgroup already exhibiting the problem condition is population-at-_____.","answer":"need","set":"Set 2","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-263","question":"The 2022 Philippine NDHS ended data collection in the month of _____.","answer":"June","set":"Set 2","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-264","question":"According to YAFS5, the two most commonly used family planning methods were pills and male _____.","answer":"condoms","set":"Set 2","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-265","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “A change in the state of the climate that can be identified by changes in the mean and/or the variability of its properties and that persists for an extended period, typically decades or longer, whether due to natural variability or as a” is _____.","answer":"Climate Change","set":"Set 2","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-266","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “primary sampling unit” is _____.","answer":"PSU","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-267","question":"A _____ is an integrated and comprehensive facility that provides appropriate information, skills, and services to adolescents and young people. It is a one-stop-shop facility that aims to improve access of adolescents to appropriate information and services.","answer":"Teen Center","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-268","question":"It is the rate computed for the entire population of a specified area or group regardless of exposure to the risk of the event. The entire population is used as the denominator — _____.","answer":"Crude Rate","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-269","question":"What percentage reported some difficulty meeting household expenses? — _____.","answer":"34%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-270","question":"What methodology is used as the study’s main qualitative method? — _____.","answer":"Narrative inquiry","set":"Set 2","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-271","question":"Occurs when a country’s fertility rate declines to or below replacement level (2.1 children per woman), yet the population size continues to grow due to the age structure of the population — _____.","answer":"Population Momentum","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-272","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The number of in-migrant per 1,000 population” is _____.","answer":"In-migration rate","set":"Set 2","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-273","question":"The probability of dying between birth and the fifth birthday — _____.","answer":"Under-5 mortality","set":"Set 2","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-274","question":"The 2021 population of Filipino male youth aged 15–24 was _____ million.","answer":"10.3","set":"Set 2","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-275","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “Includes: oral contraceptive pills; female and male sterilization; IUD; injectables; implants; condom; and, natural FP methods such as cervical mucus, basal body temperature method (BBT), symptothermal method, standard days method (SDM)” is _____.","answer":"Modern family planning","set":"Set 2","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-276","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “standard error” is _____.","answer":"SE","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-277","question":"In the Philippines, under RA No. _____, child pornography is illegal. The law guarantees to protect children, those who are below 18 years old, from being used in pornographic performances and materials, and being induced or coerced to engage or be involved in pornography through whatever means.","answer":"9775","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-278","question":"Main Source of Data which purpose is to gather information on the health status of women particularly in the area of reproduction. Results were published in 1993 — _____.","answer":"Safe Motherhood Survey","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-279","question":"What percentage were diagnosed with arthritis, neuralgia, or rheumatism? — _____.","answer":"18%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-280","question":"What research approach did ACERT use to study nuptiality and cohabitation? — _____.","answer":"A qualitative approach","set":"Set 2","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-281","question":"Given the declining fertility level, improving life expectancy and declining mortality, the natural increase of population of the country is likewise at a downward trend. This paves the way for the country towards the _____ phase of demographic transition where both fertility and mortality are declining.","answer":"third","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-282","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “pertains to the movement of population into or out of an area in a given period for the purpose of establishing residence” is _____.","answer":"Migration","set":"Set 2","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-283","question":"On the NDHS 2022 drinking-water service ladder, the level described as “Drinking water from an unprotected dug well or unprotected spring” is _____.","answer":"Unimproved","set":"Set 2","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-284","question":"The number of youth aged 15–24 in Central Luzon was approximately _____ million.","answer":"2.3","set":"Set 2","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-285","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The knowledge and capacities developed by governments, professional response and recovery organizations, communities and individuals to effectively anticipate, respond to, and recover from, the Impacts of likely, imminent or current hazard” is _____.","answer":"Disaster preparedness","set":"Set 2","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-286","question":"The factors that compel people to leave a city or municipality are called _____.","answer":"push factors","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-287","question":"Standard Days Method (SDM) is based on calculated fertile and infertile periods for menstrual cycles that range from 26 to 32 days. This method uses a device, color-coded “_____” to mark the fertile and infertile days of the menstrual cycle.","answer":"cycle beads","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-288","question":"It is to determine the extent of the occurrence of an event in a population within a specific time period. It is used to denote the dynamics of change involving the demographic processes — _____.","answer":"Rate","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-289","question":"What was the average age at first heart attack? — _____.","answer":"58 years","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-290","question":"What two female age groups were selected for the study? — _____.","answer":"20-24 and 25-29","set":"Set 2","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-291","question":"The Philippine demographics, particularly its population size, have been evolving at a seemingly _____ pace, from a three-percent annual growth rate in the 1970’s that was the highest not only in Southeast Asia, but the rest of the world then.","answer":"slow","set":"Set 2","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-292","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “this involves a discussion with small group of key stakeholders using a focused question regarding a specific issue” is _____.","answer":"Focus-Group-Discussion","set":"Set 2","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-293","question":"On the NDHS 2022 drinking-water service ladder, the level described as “Drinking water from an improved source, provided either water is on the premises or round-trip collection time is 30 minutes or less” is _____.","answer":"Basic","set":"Set 2","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-294","question":"YAFS5 reported the ideal interval between births as _____ years.","answer":"3","set":"Set 2","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-295","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The systematic administration of activities which provide for segregation at source, segregated transportation, storage, transfer, processing, treatment, and disposal of solid waste and all other waste management activities which do not” is _____.","answer":"Solid Waste Management","set":"Set 2","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-296","question":"A physical movement of people involving a change of usual residence from one state or territory to another during a specified period of observation for economic, social, political and/or cultural reasons — _____.","answer":"International Migration","set":"Set 2","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-297","question":"The _____ is an elastic canal, leading from the vulva to the cervix and uterus. During sexual intercourse, it functions as the receptacle for the penis and carries sperm to the uterus and fallopian tubes. During childbirth, it acts as the birth canal to conduct the fetus from the uterus and out of the mother’s body. It also provides a passageway for menstrual flow from the uterus and for urine from the bladder to exit outside the body.","answer":"vagina","set":"Set 2","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-298","question":"Main Source of Data which is a yearly publication that contains statistics which are derived from the documents used in registering births, deaths, foetal deaths, marriages, annulments, change of names, among others — _____.","answer":"Vital Statistics Report","set":"Set 2","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-299","question":"What was the Wave 2 response rate? — _____.","answer":"93%","set":"Set 2","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-300","question":"Whose Critical Discourse Analysis framework does the study employ? — _____.","answer":"Fairclough (2003)","set":"Set 2","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-301","question":"_____ are fertile every day throughout their life.","answer":"Males","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-302","question":"According to the Nagi measures, what percentage had difficulty with at least one of the 10 identified activities? — _____.","answer":"65%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-303","question":"_____ combines BOM and BBT together with other signs such as breast engorgement and unilateral abdominal pain.","answer":"Symptothermal Methods (STM)","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-304","question":"Among those receiving long-term care, what percentage received care daily? — _____.","answer":"93%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-305","question":"_____ is a dimension of life. It is experienced in thoughts, feelings, and practices.","answer":"Sexuality","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-306","question":"Approximately what percentage had experienced a heart attack? — _____.","answer":"Nearly 5%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-307","question":"_____ is an interest in “sexual objects or activities, or as a wish, or drive to seek out sexual objects or to engage in sexual activities.","answer":"Sexual desire","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-308","question":"How many children do older Filipinos have on average? — _____.","answer":"About 5.5 children","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-309","question":"_____ is the affectionate or loving personal relationship with someone.","answer":"Intimacy","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-310","question":"How many siblings of older Filipinos are still living on average? — _____.","answer":"About three","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-311","question":"_____ is the only perfect food for a baby, especially for a newborn.","answer":"Breastmilk","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-312","question":"What disrupted the original schedule of the Wave 2 fieldwork? — _____.","answer":"The COVID-19 pandemic","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-313","question":"_____ means the growth of an adolescent’s ability to think and reason. This growth happens differently during adolescent years.","answer":"Cognitive development","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-314","question":"What national law is cited as mandating health insurance coverage for senior citizens aged 60 and over? — _____.","answer":"RA 7432","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-315","question":"_____ refers to people who are attracted to same sex.","answer":"Homosexual","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-316","question":"_____, which is classified as entirely urban.","answer":"NCR","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-317","question":"“_____” means the body suddenly grows at a rapid rate.","answer":"Growth spurt","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-318","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of Filipinos intended to migrate in the coming five years.","answer":"14%","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-319","question":"An _____ is an intentional removal of the fetus from the uterus.","answer":"induced abortion","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-320","question":"What percentage experienced edentulism? — _____.","answer":"32%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-321","question":"Day 0 of pregnancy is _____.","answer":"Fertilization","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-322","question":"Executive Order No. _____ (s. 2018) renamed the POPCOM as the Commission on Population and Development (CPD).","answer":"71","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-323","question":"Day 6-7 of pregnancy is _____.","answer":"Blastocyst Implantation","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-324","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of households had or previously had an OFW member.","answer":"12%","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-325","question":"For boys, the first manifestation of changes often happen a little later than they do for girls, somewhere between _____ years.","answer":"10 and 12","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-326","question":"In computing the Age-Specific Death Rate (ASDR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"1,000","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-327","question":"HIV stands for _____.","answer":"Human Immunodeficiency Virus","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-328","question":"What percentage had difficulty standing up from a bed or sitting down in a chair? — _____.","answer":"11%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-329","question":"In fostering your cognitive development be CRITICAL of things around you – thinking before doing. L stand for _____.","answer":"Listen","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-330","question":"The _____ Region has the highest proportion of population with 14.8% while the NCR has 12.4%.","answer":"CALABARZON","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-331","question":"Oil glands produce more oil called _____.","answer":"sebum","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-332","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of migrants' first international moves were financed by family.","answer":"40%","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-333","question":"Poor or negative body image leads to INSECURE self. E stand for _____.","answer":"Excessive self-consciousness","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-334","question":"In computing the Infant Mortality Rate (IMR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"1,000","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-335","question":"Pregnancy is divided into three periods of about three months each, called _____.","answer":"trimesters","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-336","question":"What percentage lost more than 3 kg in the 3 months preceding the survey? — _____.","answer":"5%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-337","question":"SHAPE Module _____ tackles emotional changes at puberty which are often not given enough attention in sexuality education.","answer":"2","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-338","question":"The results of the 2022 NDHS also showed a slight increase in infant mortality from 21 in 2017 to _____ in 2022.","answer":"22","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-339","question":"The _____ is located at the base of our skull at the back of our head.","answer":"pituitary gland","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-340","question":"In the 2018 NMS, the median cash remittance received was PhP _____.","answer":"26,000","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-341","question":"The eggs are so __________ that they cannot be seen by the naked eye.","answer":"small","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-342","question":"In computing the Population Growth Rate (PGR) using Arithmetic Change, what does r stand for? — _____.","answer":"Rate of growth","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-343","question":"The members of the ISDN are connected through a _____ which ensures the continuum of information and services needed by the adolescents.","answer":"referral system","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-344","question":"What percentage of liabilities are personal loans? — _____.","answer":"30%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-345","question":"The sebaceous or _____ in your skin become enlarged and more active, producing excess amounts of an oily substance called sebum.","answer":"oil glands","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-346","question":"Defined as those aged 15 to 64 — _____.","answer":"working-age population","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-347","question":"There are more youth who are in a “_____” arrangement than are formally married.","answer":"live-in","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-348","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of children younger than 6 months were exclusively breastfed.","answer":"41%","set":"Set 3","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-349","question":"Too early pregnancy puts you at risk of having DISRUPTED dreams and aspirations. D stands for _____.","answer":"Dropping-out of school","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-350","question":"The 2018 NMS was the _____ nationwide migration survey in the Philippines.","answer":"first","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-351","question":"You need to be aware of your _____ to make you more responsible in expressing your sexuality.","answer":"fertility","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-352","question":"In computing the Population Growth Rate (PGR) using Geometric Change, what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-353","question":"Early signs of pregnancy differ from woman to woman and between pregnancies. These include: (No. 4) — _____.","answer":"frequent urination","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-354","question":"What percentage of older Filipinos were current alcohol drinkers? — _____.","answer":"22%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-355","question":"Early signs of pregnancy differ from woman to woman and between pregnancies. These include: (No. 9) — _____.","answer":"changes in appetite","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-356","question":"This is the phase when the number of productive working age population is the highest — _____.","answer":"second / 2nd","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-357","question":"It is the quality or character of a particular person or thing that distinguishes them from others of the same kind — _____.","answer":"Individuality","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-358","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of married women were using a contraceptive method.","answer":"58%","set":"Set 3","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-359","question":"Percent of adolescents (10-19 years old) who have begun childbearing in 2013 — _____.","answer":"13.6%","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-360","question":"AmBisyon Natin is the Philippine national vision for the year _____.","answer":"2040","set":"Set 3","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-361","question":"Percentage of youth who are idle according to YAFS4 — _____.","answer":"7%","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-362","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Cordillera Administrative Region” is _____.","answer":"CAR","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-363","question":"Situations where you might feel pressured to follow your peers. No. 2 — _____.","answer":"Smoking","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-364","question":"It is a group of people sharing a common demographic experience and this group may be observed through time — _____.","answer":"Cohort","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-365","question":"The larynx or voice box gets larger and sticks out at the front of the throat — _____.","answer":"Adam’s apple","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-366","question":"What percentage of surviving older persons were receiving long-term care? — _____.","answer":"12%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-367","question":"These are devices that mechanically prevent fertilization — _____.","answer":"Barrier Methods","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-368","question":"According to the 2017 NDHS, what percentage of women aged 15-49 were never married? — _____.","answer":"36%","set":"Set 3","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-369","question":"Ways to manage stress. No. 1 — _____.","answer":"Get enough sleep","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-370","question":"Among the 17 administrative regions of the country, _____ regions have a contraceptive prevalence rate (CPR) for modern family planning methods that are lower than the national level.","answer":"four / 4","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-371","question":"Your capacity to manage stress and emotions is important in attaining your overall health and well-being — _____.","answer":"Stress Management Skills","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-372","question":"A locality’s number of males per 100 females is measured by the _____ ratio.","answer":"sex","set":"Set 3","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-373","question":"_____ fuels the cycle of poverty and discrimination. It has been labeled an epidemic that forces girls to drop out of school. It has reached national calamity status.","answer":"Teenage Pregnancy","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-374","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of women aged 15–24 had thorough HIV prevention knowledge.","answer":"26%","set":"Set 3","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-375","question":"_____ is determined at the time of conception (when the baby is conceived); a chromosome from the sperm cell, either X or Y, fuses with the X chromosome in the egg cell.","answer":"Chromosomal sex","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-376","question":"The first confirmed COVID-19 case in the Philippines was reported in the month of _____.","answer":"January","set":"Set 3","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-377","question":"Article _____ further imposes a higher prison term on the woman or her parents if the abortion is undertaken \"in order to conceal [the woman's] dishonor\".","answer":"258","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-378","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “highly urbanized city” is _____.","answer":"HUC","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-379","question":"Menstruation comes from the Latin word mensis, which means “month.” Most females have a period each month. This is why menstruation is also called “_____.”","answer":"monthly period","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-380","question":"It refers to the occurrence of deaths in a population. It represents an attrition or reduction in numbers — _____.","answer":"Mortality","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-381","question":"The _____ are two organs, each having the size of an almond or a grape. They produce oocytes (eggs) for fertilization and they produce the reproductive hormones, oestrogen and progesterone.","answer":"ovaries","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-382","question":"What percentage rated their health as average? — _____.","answer":"46%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-383","question":"The days just before and around the time of ovulation are the time when a girl or woman can become pregnant. These are sometimes called her “_____.”","answer":"fertile days","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-384","question":"According to YAFS 2021, what percentage of youth aged 15-24 were formally married? — _____.","answer":"3%","set":"Set 3","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-385","question":"Usually, “_____” involves feelings of sexual attraction and excitement. Sometimes this feeling is called “crush,” “romance,” or “infatuation.”","answer":"falling in love","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-386","question":"Philippines has the _____ life expectancy at birth compared to other ASEAN countries, particularly Thailand (77.3), Malaysia (76.3), Vietnam (75.5) and Indonesia (71.9).","answer":"lowest","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-387","question":"_____ are usually persons who have the same age or slightly older than the group or persons with whom they are working. They may work with adults such as teachers or organizations or may implement educational activities on their own.","answer":"Peer educators","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-388","question":"Fertility, mortality and migration are population _____.","answer":"Processes","set":"Set 3","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-389","question":"_____ is respecting and valuing yourself as a worthwhile human being, honestly seeing your good and not-so-good qualities, and taking care of and nurturing yourself so you can become all that you are capable of being.","answer":"Self-esteem","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-390","question":"The 2022 NDHS infant mortality rate was _____ deaths per 1,000 live births.","answer":"22","set":"Set 3","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-391","question":"An _____ is the removal or expulsion of an embryo or fetus from the uterus, resulting in or caused by its death. This can occur spontaneously as a miscarriage, or be artificially induced through chemical, surgical or other means.","answer":"abortion","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-392","question":"According to YAFS5, _____ of BARMM youth were current drinkers.","answer":"2%","set":"Set 3","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-393","question":"The _____ is a tube that runs from the bladder through the penis. It is the passageway through which semen travels out of the body during ejaculation. It is also the passageway of urine out of the body.","answer":"urethra","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-394","question":"The Philippine Identification System Act is Republic Act _____.","answer":"11055","set":"Set 3","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-395","question":"Symptoms for Women: Painful sores on the genitalia; swollen lymph nodes on the groin. Women are often asymptomatic. Symptoms for Men: Painful sores on the genitalia; swollen lymph nodes on the groin — _____.","answer":"Chancroid","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-396","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “money transfer operations” is _____.","answer":"MTO","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-397","question":"_____ gathers information that measures how well program activities are performed based on its intended outcomes and impact. It aims to measure the quality of program implementation and to assess coverage and its impact on the change in behaviors of adolescents.","answer":"Evaluation","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-398","question":"Proportion of Female Births to Male Births = 0.4854 — _____.","answer":"2.0","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-399","question":"What percentage rely on remittances from children living in the Philippines? — _____.","answer":"58%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-400","question":"How did participants generally describe cohabitation in their immediate communities? — _____.","answer":"As normal","set":"Set 3","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-401","question":"Characterized by markedly declining mortality and fertility rates, resulting in the shrinking of the dependent age (0-14) group and expanding of the workforce (ages 15-64) — _____.","answer":"Demographic Transition","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-402","question":"The crude death rate is abbreviated _____.","answer":"CDR","set":"Set 3","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-403","question":"The 2022 NDHS total fertility rate was _____ children per woman.","answer":"1.9","set":"Set 3","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-404","question":"According to YAFS5, the contraceptive prevalence rate among youth was _____.","answer":"26%","set":"Set 3","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-405","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The frequency of disease and illness, injuries, and disabilities in a population” is _____.","answer":"Morbidity","set":"Set 3","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-406","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “overseas Filipinos” is _____.","answer":"OF","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-407","question":"_____ is the kind of influence that makes you do things that have positive impact on yourself and to others. It makes you do things that can make you feel proud, make you feel good about yourself, make other people feel happy and proud. It pushes you to have positive behaviors that enables you to be a good person and to achieve your aspirations and potentials.","answer":"Positive peer pressure","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-408","question":"It is the absolute number of population or demographic event. It is raw data which may be considered as a measure itself or used as basis for the derivation of another measure — _____.","answer":"Count","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-409","question":"What percentage reported difficulty climbing steps? — _____.","answer":"45%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-410","question":"How many male participants were included for triangulation? — _____.","answer":"16 male participants","set":"Set 3","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-411","question":"But now, the country’s population is only growing at a pace of 1.6% annually. With more than 109 million people, however, the country still occupies the _____ place in the world’s population size (UNDESA, 2022).","answer":"13th","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-412","question":"The maternal mortality ratio is abbreviated _____.","answer":"MMR","set":"Set 3","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-413","question":"The 2022 Philippine NDHS was implemented by the _____.","answer":"PSA","set":"Set 3","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-414","question":"According to YAFS5, youth drug use fell to _____ by 2021.","answer":"0.1%","set":"Set 3","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-415","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “Refers to a cluster of facilities that includes solid waste transfer station or sorting station, drop-off center, a composting facility, and a recycling facility. (RA No. 9003, 2000)” is _____.","answer":"Materials Recovery Facility","set":"Set 3","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-416","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “probability proportional to size” is _____.","answer":"PPS","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-417","question":"Apocrine glands only becomes active when you start puberty. They are mostly located under your arms and in your genital area. They produce a different kind of perspiration, which can smell unpleasant when it comes in contact with bacteria on the skin. This smell is known as _____.","answer":"body odor","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-418","question":"It refers to the live births that occur within a population. It represents additions to the population and results in the restoration of the population — _____.","answer":"Fertility","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-419","question":"What percentage reported weight loss of 1-3 kg in the 3 months preceding the survey? — _____.","answer":"19%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-420","question":"What contemporary relationship direction does the Executive Summary describe as becoming common among Filipino couples? — _____.","answer":"Cohabitation","set":"Set 3","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-421","question":"A barangay is classified as _____ if it meets any of the following: (1) has a population size of 5,000 or more; or (2) has at least one establishment with a minimum of 100 employees; or (3) has five or more establishments with 10 to 99 employees, and five or more facilities within the two kilometer radius from the barangay hall.","answer":"urban","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-422","question":"The total fertility rate is abbreviated _____.","answer":"TFR","set":"Set 3","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-423","question":"The probability of dying between birth and the first birthday — _____.","answer":"Infant mortality","set":"Set 3","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-424","question":"The approximate proportion of Filipinos aged 15–24 in 2021 was _____.","answer":"19%","set":"Set 3","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-425","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “A situation when all people, at all times, have physical and economic access to sufficient, safe and nutritious food that meets their dietary needs and food preferences for an active and healthy life. (World Food Summit, 1996)” is _____.","answer":"Food security","set":"Set 3","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-426","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Statistical Survey Review and Clearance System” is _____.","answer":"SSRCS","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-427","question":"In the Philippines, under RA No. 9775, child pornography is illegal. The law guarantees to protect children, those who are below _____ years old, from being used in pornographic performances and materials, and being induced or coerced to engage or be involved in pornography through whatever means.","answer":"18","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-428","question":"It is a given number usually expressed as k in the formula. It is used to make measure more understandable or meaningful. The rare the event one wishes to measure, the greater the value of k — _____.","answer":"Constant","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-429","question":"What percentage were diagnosed with cataracts? — _____.","answer":"19%","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-430","question":"What percentage of never-married women were reported to find it hard to get money for treatment? — _____.","answer":"39.9%","set":"Set 3","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-431","question":"Moreover, the emerging population dynamics in the country now calls for all interventions to focus more on “_____” rather than simply “human numbers” - underscoring efforts to improve people’s lives and increase respect for their human rights, including reproductive health rights.","answer":"human lives","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-432","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The number of residents who migrated out of a locality per 1,000 population” is _____.","answer":"Out-migration rate","set":"Set 3","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-433","question":"On the NDHS 2022 sanitation service ladder, the level described as “Use of improved facilities that are not shared with other households” is _____.","answer":"Basic","set":"Set 3","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-434","question":"YAFS stands for Young Adult Fertility and _____.","answer":"Sexuality","set":"Set 3","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-435","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “Refers to a set of socially ascribed characteristics, norms, roles, attitudes, values, and expectations identifying the social behavior of men and women, and the relations between them. (RA 11313)” is _____.","answer":"Gender","set":"Set 3","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-436","question":"A Filipino who is outside of the Philippines at the time of interviewer’s visit — _____.","answer":"Overseas Filipino (OF)","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-437","question":"The _____ are a pair of glands that are positioned below the urinary bladder and lateral to the vas deferens. Each of this consists of a single tube folded and coiled on itself, with occasional diverticula in its wall. They produce and store fluid that will eventually become semen.","answer":"seminal vesicles","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-438","question":"It is used to determine the relation of one sub-group to a larger group that includes the subgroup itself. It is a special type of ratio in which the denominator includes the numerator — _____.","answer":"Proportion","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-439","question":"What was the main reason for difficulty accessing healthcare services? — _____.","answer":"Financial reasons","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-440","question":"What shared experience was reported by both male and female cohabiting participants? — _____.","answer":"Sharing of responsibilities","set":"Set 3","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-441","question":"The Philippine Population and Development Plan of Action’s (PPD-POA’s) goal is to optimize _____ and address persistent population issues and challenges to reap demographic dividend and accelerate sustainable and inclusive development at all levels.","answer":"demographic opportunities","set":"Set 3","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-442","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “refers to the subgroup of the population-at-need who actually avail or of take advantage of the project services and project resources” is _____.","answer":"Population-at-demand","set":"Set 3","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-443","question":"On the NDHS 2022 drinking-water service ladder, the level described as “Drinking water from an improved water source that is located on the premises, available when needed and free from fecal and priority chemical contamination” is _____.","answer":"Safely managed","set":"Set 3","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-444","question":"YAFS5 said cigarette smoking was most prevalent in Western and Central _____.","answer":"Visayas","set":"Set 3","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-445","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The probability of dying between birth and age one, expressed as the number of infant deaths or deaths occurring before reaching 12 months of life in a given period per 1,000 live births” is _____.","answer":"Infant mortality rate","set":"Set 3","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-446","question":"Of the three processes that influence the size, composition, and distribution of the Philippine population, _____ is the most complex because unlike birth or death - which both occur only once during the lifetime of a person – it is a repeatable event.","answer":"migration","set":"Set 3","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-447","question":"The _____ prevents sperm from meeting the egg by causing a chemical change that damages sperm and cell before they can meet. It has long lasting effectiveness (12 years). Insertion and removal of the device is done by a trained service provider.","answer":"Intrauterine Device (IUD)","set":"Set 3","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-448","question":"Main Source of Data which provides small area statistics and overview of the province, its physical characteristics, demographic and socio-economic profile. The first editions of which was in 1991 — _____.","answer":"Provincial Profile","set":"Set 3","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-449","question":"Where did most older persons receive pneumococcal or influenza vaccinations? — _____.","answer":"Barangay health stations","set":"Set 3","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-450","question":"What urban research site represented Luzon/NCR? — _____.","answer":"San Juan City","set":"Set 3","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-451","question":"_____ are fertile only on certain days of each menstrual cycle and these are only the days when they can become pregnant.","answer":"Females","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-452","question":"According to the Washington Group Short Set, what was the most commonly reported difficulty? — _____.","answer":"Climbing steps","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-453","question":"_____ contain only the hormone progestin, which is like the natural hormone progesterone in a woman’s body.","answer":"Progestin-Only Contraceptives","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-454","question":"Among those who experience pain, what percentage describe it as moderate? — _____.","answer":"58%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-455","question":"_____ is a set of attitudes and beliefs about who we are.","answer":"Identity","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-456","question":"Approximately what share experienced a fall in the past 12 months? — _____.","answer":"Nearly one-fourth","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-457","question":"_____ is characterized by congruence between inner states (beliefs, feelings, attitudes) and outer states (behavior, relationships, health).","answer":"High self-esteem","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-458","question":"How many informants of deceased respondents were interviewed in Wave 2? — _____.","answer":"1,514","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-459","question":"_____ is the biological changes of adolescence.","answer":"Puberty","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-460","question":"How many surviving respondents were interviewed in Wave 2? — _____.","answer":"4,011","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-461","question":"_____ is the personal sense of one's own gender. It can correlate with assigned sex at birth, or can differ from it.","answer":"Gender identity","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-462","question":"What is the average household size of older Filipinos? — _____.","answer":"About four members","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-463","question":"_____ occurs when someone forces (or attempts to force) another individual to engage in sexual activity against her/his will.","answer":"Sexual coercion","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-464","question":"What percentage ate chicken, fish, or beans three or more times per week? — _____.","answer":"42%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-465","question":"_____ refers to people who are sexually attracted to other sex.","answer":"Heterosexual","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-466","question":"About a third of the under-five (5) population are _____, a trend that has persisted for years.","answer":"stunted","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-467","question":"About _____ have a cellular phone in Filipino youth.","answer":"78%","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-468","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of Filipinos migrated during the preceding five years.","answer":"15%","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-469","question":"An _____ is an opening between the vagina and the bladder or rectum, sometimes in both, that allows urine and/or feces to leak continuously.","answer":"obstetric fistula","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-470","question":"What percentage had a caregiver prior to death? — _____.","answer":"68%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-471","question":"Day 1 of pregnancy is _____.","answer":"Fertilized Egg","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-472","question":"In the Philippines, the total contraceptive prevalence rate has increased from 54.3% (2017 NDHS) to _____ (2022 NDHS).","answer":"58.3%","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-473","question":"During ________, the semen travels through the penis and out of the body by way of the urethra, the same tube that carries urine.","answer":"ejaculation","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-474","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of households in ARMM had an OFW member.","answer":"24%","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-475","question":"For girls, _____ is the ability to conceive or become pregnant and bear children.","answer":"fertility","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-476","question":"What percentage had health insurance? — _____.","answer":"63%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-477","question":"If a girl egg cell unites with the sperm, ______takes place.","answer":"fertilization","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-478","question":"The demographic transition has _____ phases.","answer":"three / 3","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-479","question":"In making any choice or decision, you have to ACT. T stand for _____.","answer":"Take action","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-480","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of moves to a current residence in the previous five years were financed through personal savings.","answer":"55%","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-481","question":"Older adolescents are those _____ years old.","answer":"15-19","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-482","question":"In computing the Age-Specific Fertility Rate (ASFR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"1,000","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-483","question":"Poor or negative body image leads to INSECURE self. I stand for _____.","answer":"Insecurity and anxiety","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-484","question":"What percentage of deaths were registered? — _____.","answer":"94%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-485","question":"Responsible Parenthood and Reproductive Health Law (Republic Act No. 10354) was enacted in _____.","answer":"2012","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-486","question":"The slowing down of the population growth rate in the country is largely due to decline in _____.","answer":"fertility","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-487","question":"SHAPE modules were first developed in _____.","answer":"1997","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-488","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of children aged 1–14 experienced physical punishment.","answer":"39%","set":"Set 4","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-489","question":"The _____ is the first facility from which the adolescents initially sought specific information or services.","answer":"Initiating Facility (IF)","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-490","question":"In the 2018 NMS, the top preferred overseas destination was the _____.","answer":"United States","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-491","question":"The first day of bleeding is designated as “_____” of the cycle.","answer":"day one","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-492","question":"In computing the Maternal Mortality Rate (MMR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100,000","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-493","question":"The New SHAPE Adolescents Toolkit is consists of _____ interdependent modules -- a preparatory and four core modules.","answer":"5","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-494","question":"What percentage of long-term care recipients received help with food preparation? — _____.","answer":"97%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-495","question":"The sebaceous or oil glands in your skin become enlarged and more active, producing excess amounts of an oily substance called _____.","answer":"sebum","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-496","question":"Pertains to the segment of population who are 0-17 years old. (CWC) — _____.","answer":"Children","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-497","question":"These are called “_____” because they create a barrier between the egg and the sperm, making fertilization impossible.","answer":"barrier methods","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-498","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of currently married women used a modern contraceptive method.","answer":"42%","set":"Set 4","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-499","question":"Too early pregnancy puts you at risk of having DISRUPTED dreams and aspirations. P stands for _____.","answer":"Poverty","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-500","question":"The National Migration Survey covered in the reviewer was conducted in _____.","answer":"2018","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-501","question":"Younger adolescents are those _____ years old.","answer":"10-14","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-502","question":"In computing the Population Growth Rate (PGR) using Arithmetic Change, what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-503","question":"Early signs of pregnancy differ from woman to woman and between pregnancies. These include: (No. 5) — _____.","answer":"unusual fatigue","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-504","question":"What percentage of older Filipinos were current smokers? — _____.","answer":"15%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-505","question":"Examples of this are heterosexuals, homosexuals, and bisexuals — _____.","answer":"Sexual orientation","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-506","question":"_____ are the most important and critical factor in any country’s development. They are the subjects, the core objectives as well as the drivers of development.","answer":"People","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-507","question":"It refers to the fertilized egg — _____.","answer":"zygote","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-508","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of the household population had at least basic sanitation service.","answer":"83%","set":"Set 4","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-509","question":"Percent of adolescents (10-19) who have engaged in pre-marital sex in 2002 — _____.","answer":"23.2%","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-510","question":"Republic Act 9729 is the Philippine _____ Act.","answer":"Climate Change","set":"Set 4","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-511","question":"Percentage of youth who are looking for work according to YAFS4 — _____.","answer":"36%","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-512","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “enumeration area” is _____.","answer":"EA","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-513","question":"Situations where you might feel pressured to follow your peers. No. 3 — _____.","answer":"Having sex","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-514","question":"In computing the Rural Population Growth Rate (UGR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-515","question":"There are ways to be safe and responsible online, while still having fun. No. 2 — _____.","answer":"Protect your reputation","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-516","question":"What percentage of the oldest age cohort had at least one ADL difficulty? — _____.","answer":"44%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-517","question":"These are people whose gender identity differs from the sex they were assigned at birth — _____.","answer":"Transgender","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-518","question":"According to the 2020 CPH cited in the rationale, to what percentage had cohabitation increased? — _____.","answer":"14.7%","set":"Set 4","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-519","question":"What is the major effect of teenage pregnancy? — _____.","answer":"Maternal death","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-520","question":"From _____ children in the 1970s, the total fertility rate (TFR) substantially decreased to 1.9 children in 2022, which is already below replacement fertility.","answer":"six / 6","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-521","question":"_____ (in any kind of relationship, including a romantic one) refers to feelings of envy, possessiveness, vulnerability, anger, and resentment.","answer":"Jealousy","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-522","question":"About _____ countries agreed to the 1994 ICPD Programme of Action.","answer":"179","set":"Set 4","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-523","question":"_____ give people a chance to develop interpersonal skills, a chance for companionship and new experiences, and a chance to gradually get to know a potential romantic partner.","answer":"Courtship and dating","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-524","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of women had experienced emotional, physical or sexual partner violence.","answer":"18%","set":"Set 4","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-525","question":"_____ is embedded in the totality of our being as a person – our thoughts, attitude, behaviors, feelings and emotions, preferences, and in every aspect of our personality or personhood.","answer":"Sexuality","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-526","question":"The Global Innovation Index is abbreviated _____.","answer":"GII","set":"Set 4","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-527","question":"As such, more than _____ of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) targets has reference to the empowerment, participation and well-being of young people.","answer":"1/3","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-528","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “household serial number” is _____.","answer":"HSN","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-529","question":"Our _____ is a product of what we are born with and our own unique life experiences that have shaped our attitudes, feelings, and values towards ourselves and towards other people.","answer":"sexuality","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-530","question":"It is a type of migration that refers to the movement of people within the country (in-migration or out-migration) — _____.","answer":"Internal Migration","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-531","question":"The _____ is a loose bag of skin that holds and protects the testicles. It has a protective function and acts as a climate control system for the testes.","answer":"scrotum","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-532","question":"What percentage receive income from work as a source of support? — _____.","answer":"26%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-533","question":"The first yellow-colored milk, called _____, is rich in nutrients and antibodies that protect the baby from diseases and infections. It also helps to clean the baby’s gut.","answer":"colostrum","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-534","question":"According to YAFS 2021, what percentage of youth aged 15-24 were living in or cohabiting? — _____.","answer":"12%","set":"Set 4","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-535","question":"A stage in development characterized by intense physical, emotional, and social behavior changes which ends at acquisition of social roles and responsibilities toward adulthood — _____.","answer":"Puberty","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-536","question":"The 1994 International Conference on Population and Development (ICPD) in _____ was a milestone in the history of population and development and women’s rights.","answer":"Cairo","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-537","question":"_____ happens when you feel you “have to” do something that you do not usually choose to do just to belong, to be accepted, or fit in among your peers. The fear of being rejected, isolated, or teased compels you to do such acts.","answer":"Peer pressure","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-538","question":"Population movement into or out of an area is called _____.","answer":"Migration","set":"Set 4","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-539","question":"_____is an important part of any relationship, including romantic and sexual relationships. It is important for ensuring that people are consenting to engage in any activity, including sexual activity.","answer":"Communication","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-540","question":"The 2022 NDHS proportion of children put to the breast within one hour after birth was _____.","answer":"55%","set":"Set 4","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-541","question":"At the core of ISDN4AHD is a _____ that links key actions and services among the members of the ISDN to ensure the continuum of care, services, and information needed by adolescents in the ISDN area.","answer":"referral system","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-542","question":"According to YAFS5, _____ of Central Visayas youth were current drinkers.","answer":"48%","set":"Set 4","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-543","question":"The _____ is the lower part of the uterus that extends to the top of vagina. The function of this is to allow flow of menstrual blood from the uterus into the vagina and direct the sperms into the uterus during intercourse.","answer":"cervix","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-544","question":"The second Bayanihan relief law in 2020 was RA _____.","answer":"11494","set":"Set 4","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-545","question":"Symptoms: Begins with one or more painless sores on the genitals, rectum, or mouth. The second stage may produce skin rashes, lesions on mucus membranes, fever, and malaise. The latent stage begins when these symptoms go away — _____.","answer":"Syphilis","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-546","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “National Capital Region” is _____.","answer":"NCR","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-547","question":"_____ involves the use of computational, statistical, and mathematical methods to measure or quantify certain problems or phenomenon and understand how prevalent it is by looking for projectable results to a larger population. It may use primary and secondary data.","answer":"Quantitative research","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-548","question":"It refers to the total number of people in a given area at a particular period — _____.","answer":"Population Size","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-549","question":"What percentage report appliances as assets? — _____.","answer":"40%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-550","question":"How many common-law/live-in females were in the 20-24 age group? — _____.","answer":"1.2 million","set":"Set 4","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-551","question":"The economic growth experienced by a country as a result of the change in the country’s population structure. It is the product of the demographic transition — _____.","answer":"Demographic Dividend","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-552","question":"The dependent age group in the old dependency ratio is ages _____ and above.","answer":"65","set":"Set 4","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-553","question":"The 2022 NDHS urban total fertility rate was _____ children per woman.","answer":"1.7","set":"Set 4","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-554","question":"According to YAFS5, the median age at first birth was _____ years.","answer":"19","set":"Set 4","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-555","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “A single national identification system for all citizens and resident aliens of the Republic of the Philippines. (RA 11055, 2018)” is _____.","answer":"Philippine Identification System","set":"Set 4","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-556","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Overseas Workers Welfare Administration” is _____.","answer":"OWWA","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-557","question":"_____ only becomes active when you start puberty. They are mostly located under your arms and in your genital area. They produce a different kind of perspiration, which can smell unpleasant when it comes in contact with bacteria on the skin. This smell is known as body odor.","answer":"Apocrine glands","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-558","question":"What is the age group interval in computing the Total Fertility Rate (TFR)? — _____.","answer":"5","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-559","question":"What percentage reported difficulty performing at least one activity of daily living (ADL)? — _____.","answer":"20%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-560","question":"How many participants were planned per FGD? — _____.","answer":"8 participants","set":"Set 4","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-561","question":"The _____ phase is when the proportion of the working-age population (defined as those aged 15 to 64) is larger relative to the young dependents (0 to 14 years) and the older population (65 years and above).","answer":"second / 2nd","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-562","question":"The population per square kilometer is called population _____.","answer":"density","set":"Set 4","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-563","question":"On the NDHS 2022 sanitation service ladder, the level described as “Use of improved facilities shared by two or more households” is _____.","answer":"Limited","set":"Set 4","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-564","question":"Central Luzon accounted for _____ of the Philippines' youth population.","answer":"11.2%","set":"Set 4","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-565","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The annual ranking of countries by their capacity for, and success in, innovation, published by the World Intellectual Property Organization” is _____.","answer":"Global Innovation Index","set":"Set 4","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-566","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Regional Statistical Services Office” is _____.","answer":"RSSO","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-567","question":"Article ____ of the 1987 Philippine Constitution says, in part, \"Section 12. The State recognizes the sanctity of family life and shall protect and strengthen the family as a basic autonomous social institution. It shall equally protect the life of the mother and the life of the unborn from conception.\"","answer":"II","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-568","question":"It is the computation of future population numbers, given certain assumptions about the future trends in the rates of fertility, mortality and migration — _____.","answer":"Projection","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-569","question":"What percentage said household income was just enough to cover needs without difficulty? — _____.","answer":"33%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-570","question":"What event commonly led couples to begin cohabiting? — _____.","answer":"Premarital pregnancy","set":"Set 4","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-571","question":"A barangay is classified as urban if it meets any of the following: (1) has a population size of _____ or more; or (2) has at least one establishment with a minimum of 100 employees; or (3) has five or more establishments with 10 to 99 employees, and five or more facilities within the two kilometer radius from the barangay hall.","answer":"5,000","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-572","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “refers to the number of deaths in the locality” is _____.","answer":"Mortality","set":"Set 4","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-573","question":"The probability of dying within the first month of life — _____.","answer":"Neonatal mortality","set":"Set 4","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-574","question":"The average ideal age at first sexual intercourse in YAFS5 was _____ years.","answer":"23","set":"Set 4","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-575","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “An economy that is low-carbon and resource-efficient, resulting in the generation of green jobs and in improved human well-being and social equity, while significantly reducing environmental risks and ecological scarcities. (RA No. 10771” is _____.","answer":"Green Economy","set":"Set 4","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-576","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Technical Education and Skills Development Authority” is _____.","answer":"TESDA","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-577","question":"People with _____ is similar to anorexia and bulimia because a person binges regularly on food (at least once a week, but typically more often). But unlike the other eating disorders, a person with this disorder does not try to “compensate” by purging the food.","answer":"binge eating disorder","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-578","question":"It refers to the number of migrants arriving in an area of destination per 1,000 population in that area of destination in a given year — _____.","answer":"Immigration Rate (IR)","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-579","question":"What percentage were diagnosed with hypertension? — _____.","answer":"48%","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-580","question":"What percentage of women aged 15-19 were never married in the 2017 NDHS? — _____.","answer":"91%","set":"Set 4","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-581","question":"Philippines still lags behind in terms of achieving quality education for all. In the OECD’s Program for International Student Assessment (PISA) in 2018, the Philippines ranked _____ out of 79 countries. Filipino students posted lower mean averages in Reading, Science and Mathematics.","answer":"lowest","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-582","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The ratio of woman aged 15-49 to children aged 0-14” is _____.","answer":"Child-Woman Ratio (CWR)","set":"Set 4","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-583","question":"contraceptive pills, implants, female and male condoms, emergency contraception, the standard days method, and the lactational amenorrhea method — _____.","answer":"Modern methods","set":"Set 4","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-584","question":"YAFS5 is the _____ survey in the YAFS series.","answer":"fifth","set":"Set 4","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-585","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “Refers to the employed persons who express the desire to have additional hours of work in their present job or an additional job, or have a new job with longer working hours. (LFS Technical Notes, PSA)” is _____.","answer":"Underemployed","set":"Set 4","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-586","question":"All persons who stayed in the selected households the night before the interview (whether usual residents or visitors) — _____.","answer":"De facto population","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-587","question":"The _____ are two narrow, 4-to-5-inch-long tubes connecting the ovaries to the uterus. They transport the ova from the ovary to the uterus each month. In the presence of sperm and fertilization, they transport the fertilized egg to the uterus for implantation.","answer":"fallopian tubes","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-588","question":"It is an estimate of the actual population that is exposed to the risk of the occurrence of an event during the period. This is usually the estimated population as of July 1 of the relevant year — _____.","answer":"Mid-year Population","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-589","question":"What was the mean age of those who died? — _____.","answer":"77 years","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-590","question":"What term describes cohabitation when it competes with marriage for benefits and opportunities without legal commitment? — _____.","answer":"Competitor to marriage","set":"Set 4","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-591","question":"While this is considered a positive gain, the Philippines, however, is ranked 13th as the most populous around the world (UNDESA). It is also the _____ most populous country among members of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN).","answer":"second / 2nd","set":"Set 4","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-592","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “refers to the subgroup of the total population that is most likely to develop that problem situation or condition” is _____.","answer":"Population-at-risk","set":"Set 4","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-593","question":"On the NDHS 2022 sanitation service ladder, the level described as “Disposal of human feces in fields, forests, bushes, open bodies of water, beaches, or other open spaces or with solid waste” is _____.","answer":"Open defecation","set":"Set 4","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-594","question":"YAFS5 surveyed _____ Filipino youth.","answer":"10,949","set":"Set 4","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-595","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The provision of emergency services and public assistance during or immediately after a disaster in order to save lives, reduce health impacts, ensure public safety and meet the basic subsistence needs of the people affected” is _____.","answer":"Disaster response","set":"Set 4","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-596","question":"A form of geographic or spatial mobility of people involving a change of usual residence between clearly defined geographic or political units during a specified period of observation for reasons that may be economic, social, political and/or cultural in nature — _____.","answer":"Migration","set":"Set 4","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-597","question":"While most of today’s youth are hooked on the Internet through their wireless and mobile gadgets, more than _____ in five Filipino youth reported having no source of information about sex and reproduction at all (Young Adult Fertility and Sexuality Study (YAFS)), 2013.","answer":"2","set":"Set 4","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-598","question":"It refers to the length of time a particular population would double its size under a given growth rate. It has been found out that a population growing at the rate of one (1) percent annually doubles its size in 69.3 years — _____.","answer":"Doubling Time","set":"Set 4","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-599","question":"Who were the two most common caregivers prior to death? — _____.","answer":"Daughters and spouses","set":"Set 4","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-600","question":"What urban research site represented Mindanao? — _____.","answer":"Davao City","set":"Set 4","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-601","question":"_____ are ideas we have about people where we judge them without even knowing them.","answer":"Stereotypes","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-602","question":"Among households that experienced hunger, what percentage experienced severe hunger? — _____.","answer":"25%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-603","question":"_____ entails the assumption and performance of several tasks and responsibilities.","answer":"Multiple-burden among women","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-604","question":"Among those who experience pain, what percentage report severe pain? — _____.","answer":"9%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-605","question":"_____ is a time of sexual exploration and expression.","answer":"Adolescence","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-606","question":"Approximately what share had not received any COVID-19 vaccine? — _____.","answer":"About one-third","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-607","question":"_____ is expressing yourself in threatening, sarcastic or humiliating way that may offend the other person.","answer":"Aggressive Communication","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-608","question":"How many of the average 5.5 children of older Filipinos are still alive? — _____.","answer":"About 4.7 children","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-609","question":"_____ is the data already collected or produced by others.","answer":"Secondary data","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-610","question":"How many Wave 1 respondents were lost to follow-up at Wave 2? — _____.","answer":"9","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-611","question":"_____ is understood as a violation of human rights and discrimination against women.","answer":"Violence against women","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-612","question":"What is the common marital status of surviving older men? — _____.","answer":"Married","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-613","question":"_____ or our physical attributes as male and female.","answer":"Sex","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-614","question":"What percentage belonged to households receiving the Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program? — _____.","answer":"12%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-615","question":"_____ refers to social interaction with others who could become romantic or sex partners.","answer":"Courtship and dating","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-616","question":"After a steady decline in neonatal mortality rate from 1993 to 2013, it rose slightly, from 13 in 2013 to _____ in 2022.","answer":"15","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-617","question":"After implantation, the embryo (at this stage called a _____) also gives rise to an amniotic sac and a placenta.","answer":"blastocyst","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-618","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of first-time internal migrants cited employment as their reason.","answer":"46%","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-619","question":"As the sperm matures, they move from the testicles to the _______ where they will remain to mature for about two weeks.","answer":"epididymis","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-620","question":"What percentage had at least one difficulty in the seven instrumental activities of daily living (IADL)? — _____.","answer":"32%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-621","question":"Day 2 of pregnancy is _____.","answer":"2-Cell Stage","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-622","question":"Maternal mortality ratio decreased from 144 maternal deaths in 2010 to _____ in 2017.","answer":"121","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-623","question":"Every female is born with thousands of eggs in her _______________.","answer":"ovaries","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-624","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of households in Cagayan Valley had an OFW member.","answer":"22%","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-625","question":"For the prevention of STI and HIV/AIDS, observe A-B-C-D-E. A stand for _____.","answer":"Ayoko Muna! (Abstinence)","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-626","question":"What percentage lived at least 10 km from the nearest financial institution? — _____.","answer":"24%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-627","question":"In females the gonads are the _____.","answer":"ovaries","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-628","question":"The labor force participation of the males from 2020 to 2022 is _____ compared to the female.","answer":"higher","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-629","question":"In males, the gonads are the _____.","answer":"testes","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-630","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of people aged at least 15 received remittances in the past year.","answer":"16%","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-631","question":"Our _____ includes desires or feelings towards someone of the opposite sex, the same sex, or both.","answer":"sexuality","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-632","question":"In computing the Child-Woman Ratio (CWR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"1,000","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-633","question":"Poor or negative body image leads to INSECURE self. R stand for _____.","answer":"Rejection and isolation","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-634","question":"What percentage of deceased older persons lived in rural areas? — _____.","answer":"60%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-635","question":"Responsible Parenthood and Reproductive Health Law is RA No. _____.","answer":"10354","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-636","question":"The unemployment rate of women is slightly higher than men (_____ vs. 7.5) (PSA 2023, Factsheet on Women and Men).","answer":"8.2","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-637","question":"Some aspects of sexuality are matters of human rights; these are often called _____.","answer":"sexual rights","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-638","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of children aged 1–14 experienced violent discipline.","answer":"59%","set":"Set 5","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-639","question":"The _____ provides a protective fluid environment for the growing fetus.","answer":"sac","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-640","question":"The 2018 NMS reported _____ of Filipinos were lifetime migrants.","answer":"40%","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-641","question":"The first sexual activities of Filipino youth, which includes older adolescents (15- 19 years old), are mostly _____.","answer":"non-consenting","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-642","question":"In computing the Net Migration Rate (NMR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"1,000","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-643","question":"The post-ovulatory phase is _____.","answer":"absolutely infertile phase","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-644","question":"What percentage of older Filipinos had been diagnosed with at least one illness, according to the conclusions? — _____.","answer":"73%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-645","question":"The sex of the embryo is determined by the _____.","answer":"male’s sperm","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-646","question":"Pertains to the segment of population who are 10-19 years old. (WHO) — _____.","answer":"Adolescents","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-647","question":"These socially constructed expectations, roles, attitude, and characteristics are called “_____.”","answer":"gender","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-648","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of Filipino households used improved toilet facilities.","answer":"95%","set":"Set 5","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-649","question":"Too early pregnancy puts you at risk of having DISRUPTED dreams and aspirations. R stands for _____.","answer":"Repeat pregnancy","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-650","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao” is _____.","answer":"ARMM","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-651","question":"Your _____ may likewise serve as your purpose in life – the motivation for you to strive and live meaningfully.","answer":"life goals","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-652","question":"In computing the Population Growth Rate (PGR) using Exponential Change, what does r stand for? — _____.","answer":"Rate of Growth","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-653","question":"Early signs of pregnancy differ from woman to woman and between pregnancies. These include: (No. 6) — _____.","answer":"nausea and vomiting","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-654","question":"What percentage of older persons have liabilities? — _____.","answer":"18%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-655","question":"Examples of this are transgender and cisgender — _____.","answer":"Gender Identity","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-656","question":"A birth is considered _____ if the number of living children at the time of conception is less than or equal to the current ideal number of children reported by the respondent.","answer":"wanted","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-657","question":"It refers to the physiological or bodily changes that result in development of sexual and reproductive capacity — _____.","answer":"Puberty","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-658","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of the household population had other health insurance.","answer":"39%","set":"Set 5","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-659","question":"Percent of adolescents (10-19) who have engaged in pre-marital sex in 2013 — _____.","answer":"32%","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-660","question":"The 2016 executive order adopting AmBisyon Natin 2040 was EO _____.","answer":"5","set":"Set 5","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-661","question":"Percentage of youth who are studying according to YAFS4 — _____.","answer":"36%","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-662","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Government Service Insurance System” is _____.","answer":"GSIS","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-663","question":"Situations where you might feel pressured to follow your peers. No. 5 — _____.","answer":"Skipping school","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-664","question":"In computing the Sex Ratio, what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-665","question":"There are ways to be safe and responsible online, while still having fun. No. 3 — _____.","answer":"Protect your privacy","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-666","question":"What percentage of those diagnosed with diabetes were on maintenance medicines? — _____.","answer":"76%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-667","question":"This aims to let adolescents appreciate the expected changes and tasks that they may experience during the adolescence period — _____.","answer":"Teen Track","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-668","question":"According to the 2022 NDHS, what percentage of women aged 15-49 were in union? — _____.","answer":"55%","set":"Set 5","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-669","question":"What region has the greatest number of teenage pregnancies in 2015? — _____.","answer":"IV-A","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-670","question":"From six children in the 1970s, the total fertility rate (TFR) substantially decreased to _____ children in 2022, which is already below replacement fertility.","answer":"1.9","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-671","question":"_____ also referred to as In-Depth Interviews are one-on-one discussions intended to generate a picture of the individual participant’s perspective or views about the area of interest.","answer":"Key Informant Interviews","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-672","question":"Age and sex composition are classified as population _____.","answer":"Outcomes","set":"Set 5","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-673","question":"_____ involves actions and attitude that treat persons as second-class or inferior based on sex. It specifically treats women as the weaker sex.","answer":"Marginalization and subordination","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-674","question":"The 2022 NDHS household interview response rate was _____.","answer":"99%","set":"Set 5","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-675","question":"_____ is the routine tracking of a programs activities by measuring on a regular, ongoing basis whether planned activities are being carried out or expected outputs are achieved.","answer":"Monitoring","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-676","question":"The national identification system is called _____.","answer":"PhilSys","set":"Set 5","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-677","question":"At puberty, the body achieves “_____.” This means that boys and girls have become capable of reproduction. It also includes enlargement of primary sex organs.","answer":"sexual maturation","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-678","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “housing unit serial number” is _____.","answer":"HUSN","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-679","question":"People with _____ excessively eat and then try to compensate in extreme ways such as making themselves throw up or exercising all the time to prevent weight gain.","answer":"bulimia","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-680","question":"It is the method for computing the rate of growth that assumes that there are linear increases or decreases in a population — _____.","answer":"Arithmetic Change","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-681","question":"The _____ is a walnut-sized gland located between the bladder and the penis. It is just in front of the rectum. It secretes fluid that nourishes and protects sperm.","answer":"prostate gland","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-682","question":"What percentage receive pensions as a source of support? — _____.","answer":"54%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-683","question":"The landscape where adolescents are nurtured is also changing fast. The traditional family and community influences are slowly being replaced by _____.","answer":"social media","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-684","question":"According to YAFS 2021, what percentage of youth aged 15-24 were never married? — _____.","answer":"85%","set":"Set 5","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-685","question":"Many parents, however, are unable to engage their adolescent children into dialogue about sexuality concerns because of the following factors or barriers: — _____.","answer":"Unsupportive parenting style","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-686","question":"The 2022 National Demographic and Health Survey showed a rapid decline in fertility, reaching replacement level total fertility rate (TFR) of 1.9 from _____ in 2017.","answer":"2.7","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-687","question":"_____ help you to focus through your adolescence journey, to realize set achievements, and be motivated during the time when you feel you like giving up. Focusing means allocating your resources, efforts, and time more efficiently.","answer":"Life goals","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-688","question":"The 1994 International Conference on Population and Development took place in _____, Egypt.","answer":"Cairo","set":"Set 5","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-689","question":"A damaging complication of obstructed labor is _____. In this case, there is a hole between the vagina and the bladder or rectum. A female afflicted with this condition constantly leaks urine or feces and smells bad.","answer":"obstetric fistula","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-690","question":"The 2022 NDHS proportion of women who had a postnatal check in the first two days was _____.","answer":"75%","set":"Set 5","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-691","question":"It is a _____ that provides adolescents with age and development-appropriate information, values and behavior in educating others who may share similar social backgrounds or life experiences.","answer":"peer-to-peer approach","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-692","question":"According to YAFS5, _____ of youth had comprehensive correct knowledge of HIV/AIDS.","answer":"19%","set":"Set 5","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-693","question":"The _____ or outer lips cover are a pair of rounded folds of skin and adipose that are part of the external female genitalia. Their function is to cover and protect the inner, more delicate and sensitive structures of the vulva.","answer":"labia majora","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-694","question":"The Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion Act is known as _____.","answer":"TRAIN","set":"Set 5","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-695","question":"These methods regulate or stop ovulation and prevent pregnancy. These methods prevent ovulation and thicken cervical mucus, which helps block the sperm from reaching the egg. These methods do not protect against STIs — _____.","answer":"Hormonal methods","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-696","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “National Demographic and Health Survey” is _____.","answer":"NDHS","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-697","question":"_____ is a quiet, comfortable feeling of total acceptance and love for yourself — as you are. It is respecting and valuing yourself as a worthwhile human being, honestly seeing your good and not-so-good qualities, and taking care of and nurturing yourself so you can become all that you are capable of being.","answer":"High self-esteem","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-698","question":"It shows the population living in the rural areas that can be expressed as percentage of the total population — _____.","answer":"Percent Rural","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-699","question":"What percentage report having cash as a financial asset? — _____.","answer":"7%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-700","question":"How many common-law/live-in females were in the 25-29 age group? — _____.","answer":"1.3 million","set":"Set 5","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-701","question":"According to PSA Survey of Overseas Filipino Workers of 2020, the estimated number of Filipinos working and living abroad temporarily or permanently, including the undocumented, had reached _____.","answer":"10 million","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-702","question":"The dependent age group in the young dependency ratio is ages _____.","answer":"0–14","set":"Set 5","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-703","question":"The 2022 NDHS was the _____ DHS survey conducted in the Philippines with the worldwide DHS Program.","answer":"seventh","set":"Set 5","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-704","question":"According to YAFS5, the median age at first sex was _____ years.","answer":"18","set":"Set 5","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-705","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “Refers to the population 15 years old and over who contribute to the production of goods and services in the country” is _____.","answer":"Labor Force","set":"Set 5","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-706","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Philippine Standard Industrial Classification” is _____.","answer":"PSIC","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-707","question":"_____ pertain to the gathering of information about a certain topic from a selected group consisting of a number of participants usually with common characteristics. It uses focus questions to which every member of the group responds based on their opinions and experiences.","answer":"Focus Group Discussions","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-708","question":"Feature of Census where census is taken with respect to a given point in time and data are in terms of a well-defined reference period — _____.","answer":"Simultaneity","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-709","question":"What percentage reported having leftover money after meeting household needs? — _____.","answer":"9%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-710","question":"In China, cohabitation increased from what percentage in 1980 to what percentage in 2010? — _____.","answer":"4% to 40%","set":"Set 5","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-711","question":"The _____ phase of the demographic transition is triggered by an initial decline in infant mortality (death rate) but fertility (birth rate) remains high, resulting in the swelling of the youth dependency group.","answer":"first / 1st","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-712","question":"The study of human populations is called _____.","answer":"Demography","set":"Set 5","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-713","question":"Percentage of women age 15-19 who have ever been pregnant — _____.","answer":"Teenage pregnancy","set":"Set 5","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-714","question":"The 2021 Filipino population aged 15–24 was approximately _____ million.","answer":"20.2","set":"Set 5","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-715","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The assurance that food will not cause harm to the consumer when it is prepared or eaten according to its intended use. (RA 10611, 2013)” is _____.","answer":"Food safety","set":"Set 5","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-716","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “secondary sampling unit” is _____.","answer":"SSU","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-717","question":"Article II of the 1987 Philippine Constitution says, in part, \"Section _____. The State recognizes the sanctity of family life and shall protect and strengthen the family as a basic autonomous social institution. It shall equally protect the life of the mother and the life of the unborn from conception.\"","answer":"12","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-718","question":"It is the level of fertility at which women, on the average, would have only one surviving daughter each to replace them. Hence, exact replacement is NRR = 1.0 — _____.","answer":"Replacement Level Fertility","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-719","question":"What percentage said their income from work decreased during the pandemic? — _____.","answer":"23%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-720","question":"What expression does Abalos use for cohabitation in developing-country patterns? — _____.","answer":"Poor man's marriage","set":"Set 5","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-721","question":"A barangay is classified as urban if it meets any of the following: (1) has a population size of 5,000 or more; or (2) has at least _____ establishment with a minimum of 100 employees; or (3) has five or more establishments with 10 to 99 employees, and five or more facilities within the two kilometer radius from the barangay hall.","answer":"one / 1","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-722","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “refers to the number of live births that occurred in a locality” is _____.","answer":"Fertility","set":"Set 5","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-723","question":"On the NDHS 2022 drinking-water service ladder, the level described as “Drinking water directly from a river, dam, lake, pond, stream, canal, or irrigation canal” is _____.","answer":"Surface water","set":"Set 5","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-724","question":"The fifth YAFS in the Philippines took place in _____.","answer":"2021","set":"Set 5","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-725","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “consists of persons in the labor force who are reported as (1) without work; and (2) currently available for work; and (3) seeking work or not seeking work because of the belief that no work is available, or awaiting results of previous” is _____.","answer":"Unemployed","set":"Set 5","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-726","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “University of the Philippines Population Institute” is _____.","answer":"UPPI","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-727","question":"Sexual coercion is common in the context of dating and even at some group social events. This serious social problem is sometimes called “_____.” It is even more frequent when the date involves excessive drinking of alcohol, when there is little or no social accountability for one’s behavior, or when no trusted friends are nearby to turn to.","answer":"date rape","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-728","question":"It refers to the number of population per unit of land area (usually in square kilometers). This measure is more meaningful if given as population per unit of arable land — _____.","answer":"Population Density","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-729","question":"What percentages were aware of pneumococcal and influenza vaccines, respectively? — _____.","answer":"52% and 53%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-730","question":"What percentage of women aged 45-49 were never married in the 2017 NDHS? — _____.","answer":"8%","set":"Set 5","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-731","question":"Regions that displayed high level of urbanization in the past years: Region IV-A - CALABARZON (70.5%); Region XI – Davao (66.8%), Region III - Central Luzon (_____) and Region XII - SOCCSKSARGEN (55.5%). In fact, each has posted a higher level of urbanization than the national level (54.0%)","answer":"66.3%","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-732","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The total number of population residing in the locality” is _____.","answer":"Total population","set":"Set 5","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-733","question":"The average number of children a woman would have by the end of her childbearing years if she bore children at the current age-specific fertility rates — _____.","answer":"Total fertility rate","set":"Set 5","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-734","question":"YAFS5 reported the ideal age at first childbirth for men as _____ years.","answer":"26","set":"Set 5","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-735","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The concept and practice of reducing disaster risks through systematic efforts to analyze and manage the causal factors of disasters, including through reduced exposures to hazards, lessened vulnerability of people and property, wise” is _____.","answer":"Disaster risk reduction","set":"Set 5","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-736","question":"The Philippines is among the largest and leading remittance recipients in the world, ranking _____ highest after India and China (World Bank, 2016).","answer":"third","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-737","question":"The _____ is a hollow, muscular organ that rests above the bladder. It is shaped like an upside-down pear that rests above the bladder. The fertilized ovum gets implanted into the endometrium and derives nourishment from blood vessels which develop exclusively for this purpose. This part nurtures the fertilized ovum that develops into the fetus.","answer":"uterus","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-738","question":"It is the formal study of population. It is concerned with the size, spatial distribution and composition of human populations and the processes that bring changes in them like fertility, mortality, migration or social mobility — _____.","answer":"Demography","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-739","question":"What was the most common form of long-term care provided? — _____.","answer":"Food preparation","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-740","question":"What term is used for cohabitation as a short stage before marriage? — _____.","answer":"Prelude to marriage","set":"Set 5","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-741","question":"With the decline in fertility, the population is _____ leading to a shift in the age structure. The share of the young segment population has declined; the proportion of the working age population has increased, and the older segment of the population has also gradually increased.","answer":"maturing","set":"Set 5","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-742","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The total number of population belonging to ages 0-14 for every 100 population of working age” is _____.","answer":"Young dependency ratio","set":"Set 5","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-743","question":"On the NDHS 2022 sanitation service ladder, the level described as “Use of improved facilities that are not shared with other households and where excreta are safely disposed of in situ or transported and treated offsite” is _____.","answer":"Safely managed","set":"Set 5","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-744","question":"Youth aged 15–24 made up _____ of Central Luzon's regional population.","answer":"18.5%","set":"Set 5","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-745","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The ratio between the number of women who died (for reasons of pregnancy, childbirth and puerperium) to the number of reported livebirths in a given year, expressed as the number of maternal deaths per 100,000 live births” is _____.","answer":"Maternal mortality ratio","set":"Set 5","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-746","question":"A form of geographic or spatial mobility of people involving a change of usual residence within a country (region, province, city/municipality) during a specified period of observation for economic, social, political and/or cultural reasons — _____.","answer":"Internal Migration","set":"Set 5","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-747","question":"A person that belongs to the same social group as another person or group; a friend who has a similar background such as profession, age and language, lives in the same geographical area, has similar social status, etc.; and someone who can integrate oneself — _____.","answer":"Peer","set":"Set 5","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-748","question":"It the type of population pyramid which has a base that is narrower than the middle of the pyramid. It shows the result of recent declines in fertility that affect the younger age groups. It indicates moderate population growth — _____.","answer":"Constrictive Pyramid","set":"Set 5","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-749","question":"According to the discussion, social determinants can account for as much as what percentage of factors affecting health outcomes at the individual level? — _____.","answer":"80%","set":"Set 5","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-750","question":"What urban research site represented the Visayas? — _____.","answer":"Cebu City","set":"Set 5","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-751","question":"_____ are persons belonging to the same societal group based on age, sex, status, and other characteristics.","answer":"Peers","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-752","question":"Among registered deaths, what percentage had a copy of the death certificate? — _____.","answer":"56%","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-753","question":"_____ happens to everybody but it does not happen to everyone at the same time or phase.","answer":"Puberty","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-754","question":"Among those who experienced heart attacks, what percentage were presently taking medication for the heart condition? — _____.","answer":"42%","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-755","question":"_____ is how one feels, looks at, and treats his/her own body. It may be positive or negative.","answer":"Body image","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-756","question":"How many original teeth did older Filipinos have on average? — _____.","answer":"Eight remaining teeth","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-757","question":"_____ is the expulsion of semen through the penis. It is when semen spurts out of the penis.","answer":"Ejaculation","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-758","question":"How many Wave 1 respondents were reported deceased by Wave 2? — _____.","answer":"1,579","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-759","question":"_____ produce more sweat called perspiration.","answer":"Sweat glands","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-760","question":"Among modern contraceptive methods, the _____ is consistently the most commonly used method.","answer":"pill","set":"Set 6","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-761","question":"_____ signals the beginning of adolescence.","answer":"Puberty","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-762","question":"Data collection for the 2018 National Migration Survey began in _____.","answer":"May","set":"Set 6","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-763","question":"Being assertive is not about talking, it is more about being able to LISTEN. S stand for _____.","answer":"Say NO!","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-764","question":"What percentage consulted a health professional in the week before death? — _____.","answer":"43%","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-765","question":"Day 3 of pregnancy is _____.","answer":"8-Cell Stage","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-766","question":"Modern contraceptive use has increased only by two (2) percentage points, from 40% to _____.","answer":"42%","set":"Set 6","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-767","question":"From 2011 to 2015, the number of new HIV infections among adolescents has increased by _____.","answer":"230 percent","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-768","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of households in Central Luzon had an OFW member.","answer":"7%","set":"Set 6","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-769","question":"In fostering your cognitive development be CRITICAL of things around you – thinking before doing. A stand for _____.","answer":"Apply learning","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-770","question":"In computing the Crude Death Rate (CDR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"1,000","set":"Set 6","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-771","question":"Our being male and female is genetically determined through _____.","answer":"chromosomal sex","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-772","question":"What percentage had difficulty going outside or leaving the house? — _____.","answer":"15%","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-773","question":"Poor or negative body image leads to INSECURE self. S stand for _____.","answer":"Social conformism","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-774","question":"Under-5 mortality was down to _____ deaths per 1000 in 2022 compared to 40 per 1000 in 2003.","answer":"26","set":"Set 6","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-775","question":"Sweat glands produce more sweat called _____.","answer":"perspiration","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-776","question":"In the 2018 NMS, _____ of people aged at least 15 sent remittances in the past year.","answer":"10%","set":"Set 6","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-777","question":"The _____ provides the fetus with nutrients and oxygen from the mother, and carries out waste products.","answer":"placenta","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-778","question":"In computing the Out- Migration Rate (OMR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"1,000","set":"Set 6","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-779","question":"The pre-ovulatory phase is the _____ which includes all dry days after the menstrual bleeding stops.","answer":"relatively infertile phase","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-780","question":"What percentage of hospitalisation costs were covered by children? — _____.","answer":"61%","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-781","question":"The sticky liquid is _____, not urine. It contains millions of invisible sperms.","answer":"semen","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-782","question":"Pertains to the urbanization of areas around the main urban centers as evidenced by the high population growth rate — _____.","answer":"Urban Sprawl","set":"Set 6","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-783","question":"Violence against women and girls, or against individuals who do not conform to dominant gender norms, is called _____.","answer":"gender-based violence","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-784","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of currently married women had an unmet need for family planning.","answer":"12%","set":"Set 6","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-785","question":"Early signs of pregnancy differ from woman to woman and between pregnancies. These include: (No. 1) — _____.","answer":"a missed period","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-786","question":"The first Bayanihan relief law in 2020 was RA _____.","answer":"11469","set":"Set 6","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-787","question":"How to get a good sleep. No. 5 — _____.","answer":"Manage anxiety","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-788","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas” is _____.","answer":"BSP","set":"Set 6","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-789","question":"It signals the end of fertility — _____.","answer":"menopause","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-790","question":"In computing the Urban – Rural Population Ratio (URPR), what is the value of k? — _____.","answer":"100","set":"Set 6","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-791","question":"Percentage of youth who are working according to YAFS4 — _____.","answer":"24%","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-792","question":"What percentage of older Filipinos have at least one grandchild? — _____.","answer":"91%","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-793","question":"Skills - Set your goals and aspirations in life — _____.","answer":"Life Planning Skills","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-794","question":"According to the 2022 NDHS, what percentage of women were never married? — _____.","answer":"42%","set":"Set 6","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-795","question":"This is the highlight of a woman’s fertility — _____.","answer":"Ovulatory Phase","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-796","question":"Intergenerational Poverty, sometimes referred to as the “_____”, intergenerational poverty (IGP) is described as poverty that persists from one generation to the next.","answer":"Cycle of Poverty","set":"Set 6","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-797","question":"What region has the least number of teenage pregnancies in 2015? — _____.","answer":"ARMM","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-798","question":"Deaths are the demographic process called _____.","answer":"Mortality","set":"Set 6","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-799","question":"_____ involves observing daily the cervical secretions; if there is secretion yesterday or today, a woman should consider herself fertile and should avoid sexual intercourse today.","answer":"Two-Day Method","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-800","question":"In the 2022 NDHS, _____ of the household population had at least basic drinking-water service.","answer":"97%","set":"Set 6","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-801","question":"_____ means asking for what you want or saying how you feel in an honest and respectful way that does not infringe on another person's rights or put the individual down.","answer":"Assertive Communication","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-802","question":"The Philippine Development Plan for 2023–2028 is abbreviated _____.","answer":"PDP","set":"Set 6","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-803","question":"People with _____ have a real fear of weight gain and a distorted view of their body size and shape. As a result, they eat very little and can become dangerously underweight.","answer":"anorexia","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-804","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “government-owned and controlled corporation” is _____.","answer":"GOCC","set":"Set 6","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-805","question":"The _____ prepares and transmits back referral (on the lower part of the form) to the referring or initiating facility to inform them of the services provided to the clients they referred.","answer":"receiving facility","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-806","question":"It is the population living in urban areas that can be expressed as a percentage of the total population — _____.","answer":"Percent Urban","set":"Set 6","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-807","question":"Symptoms: Generally has no symptoms in its early stages. Usually leads to AIDS. People with AIDS may suffer various infections, cancers, and other life-threatening ailments — _____.","answer":"Human Immunodeficiency Virus","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-808","question":"What percentage of those diagnosed with hypertension were on maintenance medicines? — _____.","answer":"84%","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-809","question":"_____ is a central aspect of human being. It involves the way we experience and express ourselves sexually. It involves biological, erotic, physical, emotional, social, or spiritual feelings and behaviors.","answer":"Human sexuality","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-810","question":"Among young adult women in the Philippines, cohabitation increased from 6% in 1993 to what percentage in 2013? — _____.","answer":"24%","set":"Set 6","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-811","question":"The _____ corresponds to the clitoris in the female. It may fill with blood and become hard, and erect in response to sexual urge. Its reproductive function is to deliver semen into the vagina. It also functions to excrete urine.","answer":"penis","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-812","question":"The 2022 NDHS indicated the decline of the proportion of adolescents aged 15-19 who have begun childbearing from 8.5% in 2017 to _____ in 2022.","answer":"5.4%","set":"Set 6","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-813","question":"The egg and sperm join together to form one new cell. Few hours later, this new cell splits to create two cells. These cells continue to split until a ball of cell is formed. This ball of cell is called a “_____.”","answer":"blastocyst","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-814","question":"The crude birth rate is abbreviated _____.","answer":"CBR","set":"Set 6","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-815","question":"The 2022 NDHS neonatal mortality rate was _____ deaths per 1,000 live births.","answer":"15","set":"Set 6","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-816","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The proportion of underemployed persons to total employed person. (LFS Technical Notes, PSA)” is _____.","answer":"Underemployment Rate","set":"Set 6","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-817","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “National Migration Survey” is _____.","answer":"NMS","set":"Set 6","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-818","question":"_____ is a study before the design and implementation of an intervention. It looks at the individual interests, attributes, characteristics, attitudes, and behaviors of young people within the locality. It also aims to generate information about the community and contexts within which the target beneficiaries are living. It can be done through qualitative and quantitative research.","answer":"Formative research","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-819","question":"Feature of Census where censuses are taken at a regular interval so that comparable information are made available in a fixed sequence — _____.","answer":"Reference Period","set":"Set 6","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-820","question":"What percentage received a combination of in-kind and cash support from the government during the pandemic? — _____.","answer":"51%","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-821","question":"In Thailand, cohabitation increased from 6% in 2005-2009 to what percentage in 2010-2014? — _____.","answer":"9%","set":"Set 6","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-822","question":"The 2020 Philippine Human Development Report (HDR) shows that the Filipinos’ life expectancy at birth has improved significantly, registering _____ years in 2020, which is about five (5) years longer than their 1990’s expected lifespan.","answer":"71.4","set":"Set 6","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-823","question":"The subgroup with a high likelihood of developing a problem is the population-at-_____.","answer":"risk","set":"Set 6","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-824","question":"The 2022 NDHS under-five mortality rate was _____ deaths per 1,000 live births.","answer":"26","set":"Set 6","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-825","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “A dangerous phenomenon, substance, human activity or condition that may cause loss of life, injury or other health impacts, property damage, loss of livelihood and services, social and economic disruption, or environmental damage” is _____.","answer":"Hazard","set":"Set 6","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-826","question":"In the 2018 National Migration Survey glossary, the abbreviation for “Philippine Standard Occupational Classification” is _____.","answer":"PSOC","set":"Set 6","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-827","question":"_____ tread a critical journey from childhood to adulthood. Their journey covers the period after childhood and before adulthood along the age range of 10-19 years (WHO, 2010). It starts with bodily changes at puberty, a stage in development characterized by intense physical, emotional, and social behavior changes which ends at acquisition of social roles and responsibilities toward adulthood.","answer":"Adolescents","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-828","question":"It is the method for computing the rate of growth that assumes an instantaneous growth rate, meaning compounding is done continuously — _____.","answer":"Exponential Change","set":"Set 6","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-829","question":"What percentage reported household hunger in the 3 months before the survey? — _____.","answer":"7%","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-830","question":"What future marriage option did some participants hope could reduce logistical burdens? — _____.","answer":"Mass weddings","set":"Set 6","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-831","question":"A form of spatial or geographic mobility of people involving a change of usual place of residence between clearly defined geographic or political units (such as country and other political/geographic territory for _____) during a specified period of observation for a reason such as economic, social, political and cultural. (PSA Board Resolution No. 08 series of 2017)","answer":"international migration","set":"Set 6","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-832","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The number of males for every 100 females in the locality” is _____.","answer":"Sex Ratio","set":"Set 6","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-833","question":"The probability of dying between the first and the fifth birthday — _____.","answer":"Child mortality","set":"Set 6","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-834","question":"According to YAFS5, modern family planning use among youth was _____.","answer":"23%","set":"Set 6","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-835","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “The potential disaster losses in lives, health status, livelihood, assets and services, which could occur to a particular community or a Society over some specified future time period. (RA 10121)” is _____.","answer":"Disaster risk","set":"Set 6","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-836","question":"_____ is the “migration that has occurred between birth and the time of the census or survey.","answer":"Lifetime migration","set":"Set 6","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-837","question":"SHAPE Module _____ centers on building important attitude and skills that adolescents need to have a safe, healthy, and happy journey to adulthood which include: building or improving self-esteem; keeping one’s body clean, tidy, and fit; being respectful and responsible in romantic and sexual relationships; using the internet safely and responsibly; communicating assertively; and making better choices.","answer":"4","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-838","question":"It is the method of counting wherein all persons are enumerated according to their usual place of residence. In this approach, one does not need to do the census fast. Censuses in the Philippines use this approach — _____.","answer":"De Jure","set":"Set 6","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-839","question":"What percentage used inpatient care in the 12 months before death? — _____.","answer":"39%","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-840","question":"What term is used when cohabitation functions in place of marriage? — _____.","answer":"Alternative to marriage","set":"Set 6","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"},{"id":"seed-841","question":"A form of spatial or geographic mobility of people involving a change of usual place of residence between clearly defined geographic or political units during a specified period of observation for a reason such as economic, social, political and cultural. (PSA Board Resolution No. 08 series of 2017) — _____.","answer":"Migration","set":"Set 6","source":"01_POPDEV_Plan"},{"id":"seed-842","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “this involves a personal one-on-one interview with key stakeholder usually a decision-maker or program implementer on certain issues” is _____.","answer":"Key-Information-Interviews","set":"Set 6","source":"02_Greenbook"},{"id":"seed-843","question":"On the NDHS 2022 sanitation service ladder, the level described as “Use of pit latrines without a slab or platform, hanging latrines, or bucket latrines” is _____.","answer":"Unimproved","set":"Set 6","source":"03_NDHS_2022"},{"id":"seed-844","question":"According to YAFS5, traditional family planning use among youth was _____.","answer":"3%","set":"Set 6","source":"04_YAFS5"},{"id":"seed-845","question":"In this reviewer, the concept described as “Waste which may (a) cause or significantly contribute to an increase in mortality or an increase in serious irreversible,or incapacitating reversible illness; or (b) pose a substantial present or potential hazard to human health or the” is _____.","answer":"Hazardous Waste","set":"Set 6","source":"05_PDP_2023_2028"},{"id":"seed-846","question":"All persons who are usual residents of the selected households, whether or not they stayed in the household the night before the interview — _____.","answer":"De jure population","set":"Set 6","source":"06_NMS_2018"},{"id":"seed-847","question":"The _____ is a long, coiled tube that rests on the backside of each testicle. It transports and stores sperm cells that are produced in the testes. A valve at the bottom of the bladder closes when the penis is erect to prevent urination during ejaculation.","answer":"epididymis","set":"Set 6","source":"08_SHAPE"},{"id":"seed-848","question":"Main Source of Data which is a canvass of all persons in a given territory at a particular period. It is also a process of collecting, compiling and publishing demographic, economic and social data for a particular period — _____.","answer":"Census","set":"Set 6","source":"14_Demographic_Handbook"},{"id":"seed-849","question":"What was the second most commonly diagnosed illness listed in the Executive Summary? — _____.","answer":"Cataracts","set":"Set 6","source":"15_LSAHP_Wave_2"},{"id":"seed-850","question":"What was the total female common-law/live-in population cited from the 2020 CPH? — _____.","answer":"6.3 million females","set":"Set 6","source":"16_Nuptiality_Cohabitation"}];
